1
00:00:20,396 --> 00:00:22,187
This isn't just a thriller.

2
00:00:23,229 --> 00:00:24,437
It's a mystery that defies reason.

3
00:00:25,812 --> 00:00:28,396
"In broad daylight,
at the heart of a political rally,"

4
00:00:28,562 --> 00:00:30,312
"I was abducted."

5
00:00:32,229 --> 00:00:36,021
"I am MLA Rohit Trivedi."

6
00:00:37,104 --> 00:00:39,312
"The cameras were rolling.
The police stood watch."

7
00:00:40,271 --> 00:00:42,687
"Thousands witnessed it..."

8
00:00:42,687 --> 00:00:46,021
"...yet I vanished without a trace."
If we don't see results, you won't get another message.

9
00:00:47,729 --> 00:00:49,271
The next news you hear
will be of my death.

10
00:00:50,729 --> 00:00:51,979
What have I ever done to you?

11
00:00:54,187 --> 00:00:55,604
'Suspicion falls on Behenji'

12
00:00:55,854 --> 00:00:57,562
'an innocent face and an ex-MLA.'

13
00:00:58,312 --> 00:00:59,479
But why would she do such a thing?

14
00:00:59,562 --> 00:01:01,646
'This was the work'

15
00:01:01,771 --> 00:01:03,229
'of either a fool or a mastermind'

16
00:01:03,521 --> 00:01:06,187
'The cameras were rolling,
but nothing was recorded.'

17
00:01:06,312 --> 00:01:08,812
'Everyone could look,
but nobody saw anything.'

18
00:01:09,271 --> 00:01:12,229
'It was clear the kidnappers
hadn't gotten far.'

19
00:01:12,271 --> 00:01:14,854
'They were holding me captive
somewhere nearby.'

20
00:01:17,396 --> 00:01:19,729
'Within just a few hours,
they called for ransom,'

21
00:01:20,021 --> 00:01:21,937
'sending the police into a frenzy.'

22
00:01:22,437 --> 00:01:24,646
Questions were everywhere...

23
00:01:24,896 --> 00:01:25,979
Answers were nowhere.

24
00:01:26,312 --> 00:01:29,396
'The kidnapper had no face,
and left no clue or trail.'

25
00:01:29,979 --> 00:01:32,146
He's the milkman.
He's the vegetable vendor.

26
00:01:33,021 --> 00:01:33,937
And this...

27
00:01:35,146 --> 00:01:36,604
He's the laundryman.
He's the garbage collector.

28
00:01:37,812 --> 00:01:39,437
'If the kidnapper is invisible,'

29
00:01:41,104 --> 00:01:42,271
'where will we find'

30
00:01:42,854 --> 00:01:44,896
'an invisible hero to catch him?'

31
00:01:46,146 --> 00:01:47,312
The most important one

32
00:01:49,021 --> 00:01:50,146
is this cable installing dude.

33
00:01:50,479 --> 00:01:51,812
- The cable installer?
- Yes.

34
00:01:52,354 --> 00:01:53,604
An invisible hero

35
00:01:54,062 --> 00:01:57,062
He may even enter your bedroom...

36
00:01:57,437 --> 00:01:59,104
yet you'll never notice him.

37
00:01:59,521 --> 00:02:00,646
"Jumper!"

38
00:02:09,062 --> 00:02:11,021
The milkman, garbage collector,
and vegetable vendor

39
00:02:11,104 --> 00:02:12,521
sit outside the house all the time.

40
00:02:12,646 --> 00:02:14,146
They're always seen saying,
'Yes, ma'am. No, sir.'

41
00:02:14,854 --> 00:02:15,604
But the cable guy...

42
00:02:16,687 --> 00:02:18,604
walks through your living room,

43
00:02:19,146 --> 00:02:20,687
your kitchen...
and straight into your bedroom.

44
00:02:20,771 --> 00:02:22,104
Brother, are you done?

45
00:02:22,146 --> 00:02:23,021
Yes, ma'am.

46
00:02:23,521 --> 00:02:25,312
- Two more minutes.
- Hurry up, please!

47
00:02:29,937 --> 00:02:33,396
- Adult program available on...
- Demand.

48
00:02:34,562 --> 00:02:37,187
Yes. If you want it,
you will get it.

49
00:02:37,979 --> 00:02:38,729
Otherwise, you won't.

50
00:02:39,312 --> 00:02:40,437
They're those kind of shows.

51
00:02:40,604 --> 00:02:43,021
The ones with adult fun.

52
00:02:49,104 --> 00:02:49,729
Hey!

53
00:02:50,604 --> 00:02:51,687
Yes, sir.

54
00:02:51,937 --> 00:02:52,646
Yes, Jumper.

55
00:02:54,104 --> 00:02:54,729
Where are you right now?

56
00:02:55,396 --> 00:02:56,312
Sir, where am I? Er...

57
00:02:56,396 --> 00:02:58,479
I'm climbing the sacred path
to the Goddess' shrine.

58
00:02:58,854 --> 00:03:00,812
Oh... you must be far away.

59
00:03:00,979 --> 00:03:03,312
No! Hail the Goddess!

60
00:03:03,396 --> 00:03:04,771
Then I'm afraid
your journey ends here, son.

61
00:03:05,479 --> 00:03:06,354
Ends?

62
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:09,062
Everyone, chant!
Hail the Goddess!

63
00:03:09,062 --> 00:03:10,896
- Louder! Hail the Goddess!
- Sir, I've come too far.

64
00:03:10,937 --> 00:03:12,396
I'm miles away from home.

65
00:03:12,562 --> 00:03:14,187
- Sir, I can't turn back.
- Hail the Goddess!

66
00:03:14,271 --> 00:03:15,854
Hail the Goddess!

67
00:03:17,021 --> 00:03:18,312
Just too busy, sir.

68
00:03:18,521 --> 00:03:19,146
What happened?
Did everyone die?

69
00:03:19,187 --> 00:03:20,604
No, sir.
They took another route.

70
00:03:20,729 --> 00:03:23,062
- No worries, son. Just come back.
- Sir, I'm almost at the top.

71
00:03:23,229 --> 00:03:24,896
- It's harder to climb down.
- Oh, no!

72
00:03:24,896 --> 00:03:26,229
Seek the Goddess' forgiveness
and return.

73
00:03:27,437 --> 00:03:28,354
Should I come and get you?

74
00:03:28,479 --> 00:03:29,646
What, sir? Hello?

75
00:03:29,771 --> 00:03:30,854
- Hello?
- Hello!

76
00:03:31,104 --> 00:03:32,021
- Sir?
- Hello?

77
00:03:32,479 --> 00:03:33,771
Sir, your voice is breaking up.

78
00:03:33,979 --> 00:03:34,479
Hello?

79
00:03:34,604 --> 00:03:36,271
Could you speak a little louder?

80
00:03:36,812 --> 00:03:38,896
Hello!

81
00:03:39,562 --> 00:03:40,437
Can you hear me now?

82
00:03:41,604 --> 00:03:42,271
Yes.

83
00:03:42,771 --> 00:03:43,521
Done climbing?

84
00:03:44,687 --> 00:03:45,937
No.

85
00:03:46,437 --> 00:03:48,854
Then climb back down.

86
00:03:49,271 --> 00:03:51,604
Or I'll throw you down
and break every bone in your body.

87
00:03:52,646 --> 00:03:52,937
Come on.

88
00:03:53,771 --> 00:03:55,021
- Sir is calling you.
- Yes.

89
00:03:55,021 --> 00:03:56,646
I'll give you a nice massage...
in boiling salted water.

90
00:03:56,812 --> 00:03:57,937
Will you hit your wife?

91
00:03:58,104 --> 00:03:59,896
- Will you hit your wife?
- Ma'am, forgive me.

92
00:04:00,021 --> 00:04:01,771
Jumper come.

93
00:04:02,562 --> 00:04:03,271
Take more!

94
00:04:03,312 --> 00:04:04,146
Kashvi ji,

95
00:04:05,146 --> 00:04:08,187
meet Jumper.
He installs cable connections

96
00:04:08,229 --> 00:04:11,104
across this area and is now
our newest police informant..

97
00:04:11,521 --> 00:04:13,021
Now then, shall we begin?

98
00:04:13,229 --> 00:04:13,687
Yes.

99
00:04:20,187 --> 00:04:21,937
When did the kidnapping happen?

100
00:04:22,646 --> 00:04:23,271
Yesterday morning.

101
00:04:23,479 --> 00:04:25,021
No, I mean the exact time.

102
00:04:25,062 --> 00:04:26,771
- Around 11:30 a.m.
- 11:30 a.m.?

103
00:04:27,604 --> 00:04:29,229
The video was uploaded online
at 2:30 p.m.

104
00:04:30,229 --> 00:04:31,521
So in just three hours...

105
00:04:31,937 --> 00:04:35,354
the MLA was kidnapped, beaten,
filmed for ransom, and the video uploaded.

106
00:04:36,271 --> 00:04:37,854
Which means they're operating
somewhere nearby.

107
00:04:38,187 --> 00:04:38,812
Wow!

108
00:04:39,854 --> 00:04:40,771
That's amazing, sir!

109
00:04:41,646 --> 00:04:44,062
What would we have done
without your wisdom?

110
00:04:45,271 --> 00:04:48,479
We should bathe you in milk.

111
00:04:48,729 --> 00:04:50,396
- Someone prepare a milk bath!
- Sir, I'm the cable guy.

112
00:04:50,396 --> 00:04:52,646
That's exactly why
I knew you'd already know.

113
00:04:52,771 --> 00:04:55,812
While searching the audio data
around the crime scene,

114
00:04:55,854 --> 00:04:58,521
we found 2111 audio files.

115
00:04:58,604 --> 00:05:00,479
Our team considered
every caller's gender,

116
00:05:00,687 --> 00:05:01,979
manner of speaking,

117
00:05:02,146 --> 00:05:05,437
and suspicious keywords,
and investigated every angle.

118
00:05:05,521 --> 00:05:06,271
That's when we found this.

119
00:05:06,896 --> 00:05:09,312
'Every road in this kidnapping
leads to one source..'

120
00:05:10,104 --> 00:05:10,812
'Tuglak.'

121
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:15,229
This call gives us
only two clues.

122
00:05:15,271 --> 00:05:17,562
One is the kidnapping.
The other is Tuglak.

123
00:05:17,687 --> 00:05:18,562
But what is Tuglak?

124
00:05:19,562 --> 00:05:21,146
A street?

125
00:05:21,604 --> 00:05:24,562
A neighborhood?
A road? A park?

126
00:05:24,896 --> 00:05:26,521
Or an entire district?

127
00:05:26,604 --> 00:05:28,021
Does any of it
sound familiar, Jumper?

128
00:05:28,521 --> 00:05:30,354
Sir, my sector has
4,300 houses...

129
00:05:30,396 --> 00:05:32,146
and over 1,700 lanes.

130
00:05:32,604 --> 00:05:34,562
But I've never heard
of a place called Tuglak. - Exactly!

131
00:05:35,521 --> 00:05:36,979
If we already knew,

132
00:05:37,854 --> 00:05:39,521
would we be sitting here
drinking tea?

133
00:05:41,104 --> 00:05:43,812
Listen, Mr. Jumper.
This is your territory.

134
00:05:44,187 --> 00:05:45,896
Isn't it?

135
00:05:46,062 --> 00:05:47,312
Search every nook and corner.

136
00:05:47,562 --> 00:05:49,937
Keep your eyes and ears open.
Find me a lead.

137
00:05:50,021 --> 00:05:51,896
Sir, this is how I keep tabs
on my neighbourhood. - What's that?

138
00:05:51,896 --> 00:05:53,562
It's a
recording bug.

139
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:57,062
It's an ultra sensitive
microphone.

140
00:05:57,229 --> 00:05:59,396
Once it's paired with the app,

141
00:05:59,562 --> 00:06:00,771
you can hear
everything inside a house.

142
00:06:00,937 --> 00:06:02,812
Once it's planted in a home,

143
00:06:03,312 --> 00:06:06,229
we'll know everything
about that family.

144
00:06:06,271 --> 00:06:08,021
Isn't that a little illegal?
It's not just a little illegal. It is completely illegal.

145
00:06:08,521 --> 00:06:12,062
You need to think like
a rogue to catch one, sir.

146
00:06:12,729 --> 00:06:13,437
Hmm!

147
00:06:13,562 --> 00:06:14,229
He's wicked.

148
00:06:14,937 --> 00:06:18,312
Ms. Kashvi, if you believe it's right,
start right away.

149
00:06:19,521 --> 00:06:21,479
But remember one thing.

150
00:06:22,896 --> 00:06:26,229
The MLA was kidnapped
48 hours ago.

151
00:06:27,521 --> 00:06:29,354
Move fast.

152
00:06:29,396 --> 00:06:31,604
Or every disconnected cable
will end up paying the price.

153
00:06:33,729 --> 00:06:34,687
Oh, my God!

154
00:06:35,271 --> 00:06:36,021
Loose connections...

155
00:06:36,729 --> 00:06:38,562
will bring everyone down.

156
00:06:38,896 --> 00:06:40,729
- You mean everyone will benefit, right?
- Huh?

157
00:06:41,729 --> 00:06:42,062
Cable.

158
00:06:45,021 --> 00:06:48,521
Ma'am, I'm certain the kidnapper
you call Tuglak...

159
00:06:48,646 --> 00:06:51,604
is hiding somewhere
in Gulab Vihar.

160
00:06:51,729 --> 00:06:52,896
How can you be so sure?

161
00:06:53,104 --> 00:06:56,521
In this neighborhood,
someone could be murdered in broad daylight...

162
00:06:56,854 --> 00:06:58,771
and no one would even
look out the window.

163
00:07:00,229 --> 00:07:02,937
It's the perfect place
to hide a kidnapped MLA.

164
00:07:03,229 --> 00:07:05,396
There are 414 houses here.

165
00:07:05,854 --> 00:07:08,437
405 of them pay
their cable bills online.

166
00:07:08,771 --> 00:07:10,812
Every payment is documented
and fully traceable.

167
00:07:11,104 --> 00:07:12,146
That leaves just nine houses.

168
00:07:12,354 --> 00:07:14,604
That's where
all the illegal activity happens.

169
00:07:19,396 --> 00:07:20,937
Sir, I'm from Jumper Cable.

170
00:07:20,979 --> 00:07:23,604
If my cable cuts out
during another match...

171
00:07:24,062 --> 00:07:24,979
I'll bury you alive!

172
00:07:26,437 --> 00:07:29,562
I've planted our little
listening bugs in all nine houses.

173
00:07:30,187 --> 00:07:31,187
We've got someone.

174
00:07:31,896 --> 00:07:33,021
He sounds suspicious.

175
00:07:34,104 --> 00:07:36,146
He's our prime suspect, ma'am.

176
00:07:36,146 --> 00:07:36,854
Ahem!

177
00:07:37,312 --> 00:07:38,312
Kohli's out, sir.

178
00:07:48,979 --> 00:07:50,187
This man is the key
to the whole case.

179
00:07:53,896 --> 00:07:54,437
Ah!

180
00:07:55,104 --> 00:07:56,437
Take your time, ma'am.

181
00:07:56,562 --> 00:07:57,812
I'll keep thinking
in the meantime.

182
00:07:57,979 --> 00:08:00,271
Why are you just sitting there?
Get up and help me.

183
00:08:03,812 --> 00:08:05,687
Would you like some tea?

184
00:08:05,771 --> 00:08:07,187
It's Bhopal's finest.

185
00:08:07,729 --> 00:08:08,437
Ms. Kashvi?

186
00:08:09,312 --> 00:08:11,312
Searching a place this small
is a waste of time.

187
00:08:11,521 --> 00:08:12,354
- Let's get out of here.
- You sure?

188
00:08:13,104 --> 00:08:13,687
Let's go.

189
00:08:14,146 --> 00:08:16,479
- Hurry up! What if he shows up?
- I told you, he won't...

190
00:08:34,896 --> 00:08:36,062
Kashvi!

191
00:09:37,771 --> 00:09:38,396
Gosh!

192
00:09:54,896 --> 00:09:55,646
Gosh!

193
00:10:02,146 --> 00:10:02,687
What happened?

194
00:10:02,937 --> 00:10:04,687
He turned out to be
a police officer.

195
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:05,312
What?

196
00:10:08,271 --> 00:10:09,187
What do we do now?

197
00:10:09,437 --> 00:10:10,854
What else?
Let's get out of here.

198
00:10:13,479 --> 00:10:14,687
Wait...

199
00:10:15,521 --> 00:10:17,521
There's a landfill
outside the city.

200
00:10:17,771 --> 00:10:19,396
Let's dump the body there.

201
00:10:19,771 --> 00:10:21,896
In a couple of days,

202
00:10:21,979 --> 00:10:24,187
the rats and insects
will make him unrecognizable.

203
00:10:24,479 --> 00:10:26,104
Isn't there any other way?

204
00:10:26,146 --> 00:10:27,062
Oh!

205
00:10:27,604 --> 00:10:30,062
I know every cop
and every alley in this area.

206
00:10:30,687 --> 00:10:33,229
If you want to get out of this,
do exactly as I say.

207
00:10:33,604 --> 00:10:34,479
Oh, no!

208
00:10:47,771 --> 00:10:49,521
- License.
- No.

209
00:10:49,896 --> 00:10:50,812
License!

210
00:10:51,062 --> 00:10:52,687
- Yes. It's here.
- Here's the license.

211
00:10:52,729 --> 00:10:53,354
License?

212
00:10:59,021 --> 00:11:01,521
Sir, what's this checking for?

213
00:11:02,271 --> 00:11:05,187
MLA Rohit was kidnapped.
We've been instructed to check.

214
00:11:06,604 --> 00:11:07,854
Where are you both coming from?

215
00:11:08,646 --> 00:11:11,396
That... Kohefiza...

216
00:11:11,562 --> 00:11:13,312
We're coming from
Kohefiza Colony, sir.

217
00:11:13,896 --> 00:11:14,479
Where are you going?

218
00:11:15,104 --> 00:11:18,187
We're going to eat
Kharbanda's 'paranthas', sir.

219
00:11:18,729 --> 00:11:19,937
- To eat Kharbanda's 'paranthas'?
- Yes.

220
00:11:20,479 --> 00:11:22,479
Then why are you sweating so much?

221
00:11:22,646 --> 00:11:23,812
Did you bathe in your car?

222
00:11:24,104 --> 00:11:26,604
No, sir.
The AC isn't working.

223
00:11:26,646 --> 00:11:29,396
Then roll down the window!

224
00:11:29,479 --> 00:11:30,812
- What's stopping you?
- Sir...

225
00:11:30,854 --> 00:11:33,229
We've been cooped up for days.

226
00:11:33,271 --> 00:11:34,396
Please let us enjoy the drive.

227
00:11:34,812 --> 00:11:37,229
- Check the car.
- Let them through.

228
00:11:41,521 --> 00:11:43,229
Let them go.

229
00:11:43,312 --> 00:11:44,521
Alright, ma'am.
You can go.

230
00:11:45,021 --> 00:11:45,646
Thank you, sir.

231
00:11:45,687 --> 00:11:47,229
Move along.

232
00:11:48,562 --> 00:11:49,854
Stop!

233
00:11:54,479 --> 00:11:55,104
Step out!

234
00:12:03,729 --> 00:12:04,521
What's in the trunk?

235
00:12:06,646 --> 00:12:07,771
Why is that cloth
sticking out?

236
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:11,062
Nothing, sir.
It's just laundry.

237
00:12:11,604 --> 00:12:12,396
Are you a laundryman?

238
00:12:12,896 --> 00:12:13,812
Yes, sir...
No!

239
00:12:13,979 --> 00:12:14,729
No, sir.

240
00:12:15,354 --> 00:12:17,104
Open the trunk.

241
00:12:17,604 --> 00:12:18,687
Now!

242
00:12:19,812 --> 00:12:21,396
Are you going to open it or not?
Open it!

243
00:12:24,187 --> 00:12:24,854
Open it!

244
00:12:26,187 --> 00:12:27,562
Something doesn't add up.

245
00:12:27,854 --> 00:12:28,312
Huh?

246
00:12:28,479 --> 00:12:29,687
Are you the kidnapper?

247
00:12:29,729 --> 00:12:30,521
Sir, we...

248
00:12:30,521 --> 00:12:32,271
We were just on our way
to eat parathas, sir.

249
00:12:33,104 --> 00:12:33,854
Open it. Now!

250
00:12:34,187 --> 00:12:35,604
Sir, I'm trying.

251
00:12:37,021 --> 00:12:37,812
Hey, Jumper!

252
00:12:38,687 --> 00:12:39,271
Where have you been?

253
00:12:40,021 --> 00:12:40,687
Where's your phone?

254
00:12:41,062 --> 00:12:42,854
Take it out.
Check it now.

255
00:12:42,896 --> 00:12:43,854
Y-Yes, sir.

256
00:12:43,896 --> 00:12:44,854
How many missed calls?

257
00:12:46,812 --> 00:12:47,687
- Sir...
- Well?

258
00:12:47,937 --> 00:12:49,396
Twelve, sir.

259
00:12:49,687 --> 00:12:50,729
Sir's been calling you
this whole time.

260
00:12:53,187 --> 00:12:53,854
Hello, sir.

261
00:12:55,229 --> 00:12:56,979
You too.
Come here.

262
00:12:59,896 --> 00:13:01,479
Gupta, what's going on?

263
00:13:04,021 --> 00:13:05,729
Are you on night duty,

264
00:13:06,604 --> 00:13:07,354
or stopping everyone
who passes by?

265
00:13:08,437 --> 00:13:09,729
They're with me.

266
00:13:10,104 --> 00:13:10,812
Let them go.

267
00:13:11,437 --> 00:13:12,021
Right away!

268
00:13:12,812 --> 00:13:13,604
Yes, sir.

269
00:13:13,979 --> 00:13:14,479
- Get in.
- Go ahead.

270
00:13:15,604 --> 00:13:16,187
Yes, sir.

271
00:13:16,979 --> 00:13:17,854
Pandey!

272
00:13:18,104 --> 00:13:19,604
Bring the old wreck.

273
00:13:25,521 --> 00:13:27,104
There are countless kidnappings
every year...

274
00:13:27,479 --> 00:13:28,646
committed by countless criminals.

275
00:13:28,771 --> 00:13:30,146
There are 365 days in a year.

276
00:13:30,271 --> 00:13:32,021
Did this one have to happen
on my day?

277
00:13:34,312 --> 00:13:35,854
Sir?

278
00:13:36,521 --> 00:13:38,479
Welcome!

279
00:13:40,312 --> 00:13:42,979
Only two people
are busier than everyone else.

280
00:13:43,021 --> 00:13:44,437
One is the Prime Minister...
and the other is you.

281
00:13:44,479 --> 00:13:46,562
- Sir, I...
- And what about you?

282
00:13:50,562 --> 00:13:54,312
I'm trying very hard
to keep my temper...

283
00:13:55,521 --> 00:13:58,979
The right questions
lead to the right answers.

284
00:13:59,021 --> 00:14:00,646
Isn't that right,
Mr. Shanti? - Absolutely.

285
00:14:02,021 --> 00:14:05,396
But look at him.
He's lost in his own world.

286
00:14:05,812 --> 00:14:08,229
One moment he's staring at the sky...

287
00:14:08,229 --> 00:14:09,479
the next, somewhere else.

288
00:14:09,521 --> 00:14:11,729
Are you even listening to me?

289
00:14:12,146 --> 00:14:15,521
Tuglak isn't a street,
a neighborhood, or a park.

290
00:14:16,062 --> 00:14:16,896
It isn't a place.

291
00:14:17,521 --> 00:14:21,396
Mr. Shanti spotted
an odd-looking man...

292
00:14:21,771 --> 00:14:23,937
hidden in the crime scene footage.

293
00:14:24,479 --> 00:14:25,937
Meet Tuglak.

294
00:14:26,812 --> 00:14:27,312
He...

295
00:14:48,437 --> 00:14:49,604
- He...
- He?

296
00:14:53,062 --> 00:14:54,646
He's Tuglak!

297
00:14:54,729 --> 00:14:55,937
A master of disguises.

298
00:14:57,729 --> 00:14:59,354
He's gone by many names...

299
00:15:00,062 --> 00:15:02,771
Ashok, Maurya,
Zafar, even Akbar.

300
00:15:03,479 --> 00:15:04,937
These days,
he calls himself Tuglak.

301
00:15:05,312 --> 00:15:08,646
In the blink of an eye,

302
00:15:08,687 --> 00:15:12,521
I had him in a headlock,
just like the actor Sanjeev Kumar.

303
00:15:17,854 --> 00:15:18,729
Mr. Shanti?

304
00:15:19,937 --> 00:15:20,854
Yes, sir.

305
00:15:21,312 --> 00:15:22,187
Isn't that right?

306
00:15:22,521 --> 00:15:24,062
He put up quite a fight.

307
00:15:24,479 --> 00:15:26,521
I was sweating so much
trying to catch him...

308
00:15:26,854 --> 00:15:28,271
that he slipped
right out of my hands.

309
00:15:29,062 --> 00:15:30,771
He got away.

310
00:15:30,812 --> 00:15:32,146
But doesn't he look
like a police officer?

311
00:15:32,312 --> 00:15:35,771
Counterfeit currency,
fake IDs,

312
00:15:36,229 --> 00:15:37,062
fake credit cards...

313
00:15:38,146 --> 00:15:39,479
those are just a few
of his specialties.

314
00:15:40,187 --> 00:15:42,521
Two months ago,
he roamed Bediya...

315
00:15:42,687 --> 00:15:44,146
posing as a police officer.

316
00:15:44,187 --> 00:15:45,854
Who exactly is this man?

317
00:15:47,729 --> 00:15:48,521
So, what have you concluded?

318
00:15:48,854 --> 00:15:50,937
Sir, my conclusion is...

319
00:15:50,937 --> 00:15:52,312
One moment.

320
00:15:55,729 --> 00:15:56,146
Yes?

321
00:15:56,896 --> 00:15:57,479
Ma'am?

322
00:16:01,771 --> 00:16:02,896
Who is that?

323
00:16:03,687 --> 00:16:04,937
- Sharma ji..
- Hello Behenji.

324
00:16:05,854 --> 00:16:08,187
I want hourly updates of this case.

325
00:16:08,396 --> 00:16:09,771
Yes. My entire team
is working on it.

326
00:16:09,896 --> 00:16:11,521
"Why hasn't there been
any progress?"

327
00:16:12,104 --> 00:16:14,521
It's a small police station.
We're short-handed.

328
00:16:14,604 --> 00:16:15,521
"Can you handle this
or not?"

329
00:16:15,687 --> 00:16:16,812
Yes, ma'am.
Leave it to us.

330
00:16:31,062 --> 00:16:31,562
Gosh!

331
00:16:42,604 --> 00:16:43,562
Hello.

332
00:16:44,271 --> 00:16:47,312
Buddy, the dead man
in your car's trunk...

333
00:16:47,562 --> 00:16:48,479
worked for me.

334
00:16:49,687 --> 00:16:51,062
Hello? Who is this?

335
00:16:51,146 --> 00:16:52,312
Can't you hear me?

336
00:16:52,896 --> 00:16:53,812
Should I climb a tower?

337
00:16:54,687 --> 00:16:55,604
Listen carefully.

338
00:16:56,479 --> 00:16:57,396
If you tell the police...

339
00:16:57,604 --> 00:16:59,896
about the body
in your trunk,

340
00:17:00,146 --> 00:17:02,021
your little viral video...

341
00:17:03,229 --> 00:17:04,187
will land you behind bars.

342
00:17:04,354 --> 00:17:06,646
Keep your mouth shut
till my next orders

343
00:17:06,771 --> 00:17:07,729
and just do

344
00:17:07,979 --> 00:17:08,896
as I say.

345
00:17:09,312 --> 00:17:10,562
What do you want from me?

346
00:17:13,812 --> 00:17:15,396
Patience.

347
00:17:23,146 --> 00:17:23,854
Mr. Shanti,

348
00:17:24,146 --> 00:17:25,646
I need to talk to you
about Tuglak.

349
00:17:29,729 --> 00:17:31,521
Didn't I tell you
to keep your mouth shut?

350
00:17:32,479 --> 00:17:34,854
One small mistake...

351
00:17:36,854 --> 00:17:37,854
and the punishment
will be severe.

352
00:17:37,937 --> 00:17:40,521
Because Tuglak is dead,

353
00:17:41,729 --> 00:17:43,187
what was meant to happen
in seven days...

354
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:44,729
will happen
in seven hours.

355
00:17:44,979 --> 00:17:46,104
Want to see my next move?

356
00:17:46,146 --> 00:17:48,979
Just watch.
Sir, the kidnappers have sent another video.

357
00:17:49,312 --> 00:17:50,354
Already?

358
00:17:50,354 --> 00:17:51,229
- Yes, sir.
- Sir!

359
00:17:51,729 --> 00:17:52,437
Sir!

360
00:17:52,521 --> 00:17:54,104
- I'm coming.
- Another video has arrived.

361
00:17:54,229 --> 00:17:54,979
The new video's here.

362
00:17:55,229 --> 00:17:55,979
Play it.

363
00:17:57,354 --> 00:17:58,521
Here's your next task.

364
00:18:00,979 --> 00:18:01,896
Rithala...

365
00:18:02,854 --> 00:18:03,812
Industrial Estate...

366
00:18:04,812 --> 00:18:05,521
Mill No. 4...

367
00:18:06,312 --> 00:18:07,562
and the rooftop...

368
00:18:08,104 --> 00:18:11,104
of the building
near Jehangir Minar.

369
00:18:12,271 --> 00:18:15,187
Every one of these places
is a drug lab.

370
00:18:15,604 --> 00:18:16,187
You'll find...

371
00:18:17,354 --> 00:18:18,771
70 kilos of drugs there.

372
00:18:19,437 --> 00:18:20,104
You have...

373
00:18:21,104 --> 00:18:22,979
four hours...

374
00:18:33,521 --> 00:18:34,271
Another ransom video...
another set of clues?

375
00:18:35,271 --> 00:18:37,062
Yes, sir.
It's on every news channel.

376
00:18:39,562 --> 00:18:41,604
This is one bizarre
ransom demand.

377
00:18:41,812 --> 00:18:43,937
Instead of money,
he wants us to catch criminals.

378
00:18:44,187 --> 00:18:45,312
Sir, we've got a message.

379
00:18:45,604 --> 00:18:46,104
What is it?

380
00:18:46,104 --> 00:18:48,021
The central forces
have been deployed.

381
00:18:48,896 --> 00:18:49,604
Sir...

382
00:18:49,979 --> 00:18:52,479
I'll take your leave.
I'm no longer needed here.

383
00:18:52,687 --> 00:18:53,479
What do you mean,
you're leaving?

384
00:18:55,854 --> 00:18:57,021
Who said
you're not needed?

385
00:18:58,146 --> 00:18:59,521
Didn't you hear?
We have four hours.

386
00:19:00,604 --> 00:19:01,812
Today is all we've got.

387
00:19:03,437 --> 00:19:05,021
We need to move faster.

388
00:19:05,771 --> 00:19:08,062
Otherwise, the national
and international media...

389
00:19:08,312 --> 00:19:09,687
the CBI, the CID...

390
00:19:09,937 --> 00:19:11,479
and every other agency
under the sun...

391
00:19:11,646 --> 00:19:13,104
will descend
on this police station.

392
00:19:13,771 --> 00:19:15,937
Understood?
There's only one way out.

393
00:19:16,896 --> 00:19:17,896
Find Tuglak.

394
00:19:18,479 --> 00:19:19,271
Find the kidnapped MLA.

395
00:19:29,604 --> 00:19:30,396
Jumper?

396
00:19:31,187 --> 00:19:31,812
Whatever you want,

397
00:19:33,104 --> 00:19:36,271
non-veg, veg, 'murgh musallam',
egg curry,

398
00:19:36,854 --> 00:19:37,854
you will get it all.

399
00:19:39,104 --> 00:19:40,396
It's a long day today.

400
00:19:41,229 --> 00:19:42,021
Please co-operate.

401
00:19:42,771 --> 00:19:44,021
Sir?

402
00:19:44,062 --> 00:19:44,896
Have some chickpeas.

403
00:19:45,354 --> 00:19:45,896
Hmm.

404
00:19:46,437 --> 00:19:47,104
What about us?

405
00:19:48,021 --> 00:19:48,979
Should I order
rajma chawal?

406
00:19:49,146 --> 00:19:50,812
Rajma chawal
will make you gassy.

407
00:19:50,896 --> 00:19:52,146
That's not a problem
during the day.

408
00:19:52,479 --> 00:19:53,521
It'll just drift away.

409
00:19:54,604 --> 00:19:55,979
It's worse at night.

410
00:20:26,646 --> 00:20:27,104
Huh?

411
00:20:28,187 --> 00:20:28,979
Jumper,

412
00:20:29,854 --> 00:20:30,396
get started.

413
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:31,187
This...

414
00:20:31,479 --> 00:20:33,104
What's this, Mr. Shanti?

415
00:20:33,104 --> 00:20:33,729
A list...

416
00:20:34,521 --> 00:20:36,062
of your cable subscribers.

417
00:20:36,271 --> 00:20:38,812
The people who trust you enough
to let you into their bedrooms.

418
00:20:39,312 --> 00:20:40,854
Find out where
this maniac is hiding.

419
00:20:40,896 --> 00:20:41,729
What am I supposed
to do with this?

420
00:20:42,229 --> 00:20:43,812
Treat everyone
as a suspect.

421
00:20:44,521 --> 00:20:45,437
Only you...

422
00:20:46,146 --> 00:20:48,146
can crack this. Understood?

423
00:20:49,687 --> 00:20:50,437
Take good care of him.

424
00:20:50,729 --> 00:20:52,187
- Help him.
- Yes, sir.

425
00:20:52,312 --> 00:20:54,271
Turn on every AC and cooler.
Make sure he's comfortable.

426
00:20:54,312 --> 00:20:55,187
They're not working, sir.

427
00:20:55,687 --> 00:20:56,729
Assume that it's working.

428
00:20:57,646 --> 00:20:58,396
- Okay?
- Sir,

429
00:20:58,604 --> 00:20:59,604
- I've got a call.
- Wait a second.

430
00:21:00,354 --> 00:21:01,146
Focus on the task.

431
00:21:01,396 --> 00:21:03,479
Ignore every call.
Switch off your phone.

432
00:21:03,812 --> 00:21:04,562
Come on.

433
00:21:04,854 --> 00:21:06,896
Turn it off. The police
and the cable network can wait.

434
00:21:08,771 --> 00:21:09,312
Hello.

435
00:21:10,437 --> 00:21:14,062
Son, buckle up, clear your mind,
and listen carefully.

436
00:21:18,854 --> 00:21:20,229
The body in your car's trunk...

437
00:21:22,729 --> 00:21:23,812
belongs to my partner.

438
00:21:26,104 --> 00:21:28,062
I'm the mastermind
behind this kidnapping.

439
00:21:31,729 --> 00:21:33,312
You killed my partner.

440
00:21:34,521 --> 00:21:37,021
So who's going to finish
what he started?

441
00:21:38,896 --> 00:21:41,187
There's a hard drive
hidden on his body.

442
00:21:42,687 --> 00:21:45,521
Find it.

443
00:21:45,687 --> 00:21:47,687
If you tell anyone about this,

444
00:21:48,812 --> 00:21:49,521
let me make
one thing very clear.

445
00:21:50,437 --> 00:21:52,729
You, that lady,
the police officers...

446
00:21:52,896 --> 00:21:56,062
even your sidekick, Splitter...
I know everything about you.

447
00:21:56,062 --> 00:21:58,604
Your history, geography,
biology, and psychology.

448
00:21:59,104 --> 00:21:59,896
Too little time.

449
00:22:01,396 --> 00:22:02,271
Too much to do.

450
00:22:05,229 --> 00:22:06,396
Find the hard drive...

451
00:22:08,021 --> 00:22:10,396
like your life
depends on it...

452
00:22:13,021 --> 00:22:15,104
because it does.

453
00:22:17,396 --> 00:22:18,979
Can I ask you something?

454
00:22:19,187 --> 00:22:20,146
That depends.

455
00:22:20,437 --> 00:22:21,271
On what?

456
00:22:22,604 --> 00:22:23,562
On the question.

457
00:22:25,396 --> 00:22:26,854
Do you really think...

458
00:22:27,104 --> 00:22:28,437
you can make me
do your bidding?

459
00:22:32,771 --> 00:22:34,396
Your cable shop...

460
00:22:36,979 --> 00:22:39,396
Its security code
is 786.

461
00:22:40,604 --> 00:22:42,979
Your email ID is
jjumpercable@gmail.com.

462
00:22:43,354 --> 00:22:45,396
The password is
todu32.

463
00:22:46,187 --> 00:22:47,187
Your Aadhaar details...

464
00:22:47,979 --> 00:22:50,354
your KYC,
your bank account...

465
00:22:52,604 --> 00:22:55,479
even the private photos
hidden on your phone...

466
00:22:55,896 --> 00:22:57,354
I have access
to all of it.

467
00:23:00,479 --> 00:23:03,312
And think about the lady with you.
You don't seem to care about her.

468
00:23:03,812 --> 00:23:04,604
Do you know...

469
00:23:05,062 --> 00:23:06,729
the difference between
the cartoons...

470
00:23:06,812 --> 00:23:08,562
on your cable network
and real life?

471
00:23:09,646 --> 00:23:10,187
What is it?

472
00:23:15,021 --> 00:23:17,229
In cartoons,
the good guys always win.

473
00:23:17,646 --> 00:23:19,021
And in real life?

474
00:23:19,937 --> 00:23:21,104
I have to admit...

475
00:23:21,979 --> 00:23:25,187
even when you're terrified,
your sense of humor is impressive.

476
00:23:25,479 --> 00:23:26,937
Why are you making me do this?

477
00:23:27,354 --> 00:23:30,062
You were simply
in the wrong place...

478
00:23:31,521 --> 00:23:33,229
Your Jumper Cable's
blaring wedding songs...

479
00:23:33,312 --> 00:23:35,437
rang in my ears
all morning yesterday.

480
00:23:35,979 --> 00:23:37,312
Only in India...

481
00:23:38,146 --> 00:23:39,187
can your celebration...

482
00:23:39,604 --> 00:23:41,271
become everyone else's misery.

483
00:23:45,187 --> 00:23:47,812
Sir, there were 2,000 calls
made around the crime scene.

484
00:23:48,729 --> 00:23:50,187
- Oh, no!
- Two thousand?

485
00:23:50,854 --> 00:23:53,229
That's like looking
for a needle in a haystack.

486
00:23:53,521 --> 00:23:56,104
Sir, if you want,
Ms. Kashvi and I...

487
00:23:56,271 --> 00:23:58,521
- can go through every number.
- We're talking north,

488
00:23:58,562 --> 00:24:00,104
and you're heading south.

489
00:24:00,146 --> 00:24:01,104
What a line!

490
00:24:01,396 --> 00:24:03,562
Why don't you do
what you suggested earlier?

491
00:24:03,604 --> 00:24:05,729
What did you say
about catching criminals?

492
00:24:06,437 --> 00:24:09,271
- Forgot already?
- Think like a criminal.

493
00:24:09,479 --> 00:24:10,937
Exactly.
Show us how it's done.

494
00:24:11,771 --> 00:24:12,354
Meaning?

495
00:24:13,479 --> 00:24:15,354
Imagine you're
part of this kidnapping.

496
00:24:21,562 --> 00:24:22,521
Me?

497
00:24:25,312 --> 00:24:28,146
I mean, just suppose
you were involved.

498
00:24:28,354 --> 00:24:30,229
What would you do?

499
00:24:32,271 --> 00:24:33,021
First...

500
00:24:33,562 --> 00:24:34,271
I wouldn't call.

501
00:24:35,312 --> 00:24:36,604
But if you had to?

502
00:24:38,062 --> 00:24:38,937
If I did...

503
00:24:39,437 --> 00:24:41,187
I'd keep it brief.

504
00:24:41,937 --> 00:24:42,979
Mr. Shanti...

505
00:24:43,771 --> 00:24:45,187
that's our needle!

506
00:24:46,146 --> 00:24:47,062
- Ms. Kashvi?
- Yes, sir.

507
00:24:47,104 --> 00:24:48,937
Make a list of every call...

508
00:24:49,187 --> 00:24:50,187
that lasted
less than ten seconds.

509
00:24:50,229 --> 00:24:50,687
Yes, sir.

510
00:24:51,896 --> 00:24:54,437
Sir, only 20 calls
lasted under ten seconds.

511
00:25:00,729 --> 00:25:01,854
Good. Get started.

512
00:25:03,312 --> 00:25:05,521
- Call each number, one by one.
- Okay, sir.

513
00:25:07,437 --> 00:25:09,229
Your chest is injured...

514
00:25:09,771 --> 00:25:11,354
yet you're bandaging your back.

515
00:25:12,479 --> 00:25:16,271
You must be the first genius
helping the police get himself killed.

516
00:25:17,604 --> 00:25:19,729
See the number on the screen?

517
00:25:19,729 --> 00:25:20,312
Yes, that one.

518
00:25:20,354 --> 00:25:23,521
The fifth number on that list
belongs to the dead man in your trunk.

519
00:25:23,521 --> 00:25:24,521
No, the other one.

520
00:25:24,562 --> 00:25:26,062
That phone's about to ring.

521
00:25:26,521 --> 00:25:28,396
The officer at the station
will hear it.

522
00:25:28,854 --> 00:25:31,687
So before it rings...

523
00:25:35,062 --> 00:25:35,604
Run.

524
00:25:36,979 --> 00:25:38,146
Run!

525
00:25:38,937 --> 00:25:39,937
- Hey, Jumper!
- Yes, sir?

526
00:25:40,312 --> 00:25:41,187
Where are you going?

527
00:25:41,354 --> 00:25:43,021
Sir, my phone...

528
00:25:43,354 --> 00:25:44,021
It's right there.

529
00:25:44,604 --> 00:25:45,562
You're holding it.

530
00:25:45,604 --> 00:25:46,396
Sir, I'm checking something online.

531
00:25:46,396 --> 00:25:46,979
Got another phone?

532
00:25:47,021 --> 00:25:48,062
It'll just take a minute.

533
00:25:48,187 --> 00:25:48,937
Is it a girl?

534
00:25:49,896 --> 00:25:51,187
- Your girlfriend?
- No, sir.

535
00:25:51,229 --> 00:25:51,812
Forget all that.

536
00:25:52,854 --> 00:25:53,812
What are you talking about?

537
00:25:54,187 --> 00:25:55,104
We don't have time for this.

538
00:25:55,646 --> 00:25:56,396
Look at sir.

539
00:25:57,021 --> 00:25:59,187
He doesn't even answer
his wife's calls.

540
00:25:59,187 --> 00:25:59,937
Hmm!

541
00:26:00,354 --> 00:26:02,771
- Mr. Shanti!
- I'm telling the truth, sir.

542
00:26:02,896 --> 00:26:04,104
It's because of a girl.

543
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:05,812
Sir, I'll be right back.

544
00:26:05,896 --> 00:26:07,271
Call the next number.

545
00:26:10,979 --> 00:26:12,937
Try the fourth one.

546
00:26:14,479 --> 00:26:16,271
- Yes, that one.
- Yes, sir.

547
00:26:16,312 --> 00:26:17,396
Yes, call that one.

548
00:26:19,104 --> 00:26:20,729
Try it again.

549
00:26:20,771 --> 00:26:21,771
- Yes, sir.
- Keep calling.

550
00:26:23,812 --> 00:26:26,854
- Don't stop calling.
- Yes, sir.

551
00:26:27,312 --> 00:26:29,146
- I'm trying, sir.
- That's the one. Keep calling.

552
00:26:36,937 --> 00:26:38,271
Turn the phone off.

553
00:26:39,646 --> 00:26:40,937
Good.

554
00:26:40,979 --> 00:26:42,312
Sir, none of the numbers
went through.

555
00:26:42,812 --> 00:26:44,187
Hmm.

556
00:26:46,896 --> 00:26:47,646
Wait.

557
00:26:48,937 --> 00:26:49,812
Search the body.

558
00:26:50,021 --> 00:26:51,604
The body? Why?

559
00:26:52,437 --> 00:26:55,771
Check his pockets,
his shoes, his socks...

560
00:26:55,812 --> 00:26:57,729
There might be
a tiny hard drive.

561
00:26:57,979 --> 00:26:58,521
Find it.

562
00:27:04,437 --> 00:27:05,187
I searched...

563
00:27:05,229 --> 00:27:06,146
but couldn't find it.

564
00:27:06,437 --> 00:27:08,521
It's tiny.
Search him again.

565
00:27:12,979 --> 00:27:14,396
Yes. Reach in deeper.

566
00:27:14,646 --> 00:27:17,021
I've checked twice.
There's nothing here.

567
00:27:17,312 --> 00:27:18,062
Check again.

568
00:27:18,646 --> 00:27:20,354
I searched everywhere.
There's nothing here.

569
00:27:20,562 --> 00:27:21,437
Did you check the cavities?

570
00:27:23,396 --> 00:27:24,896
What cavities?

571
00:27:26,396 --> 00:27:28,021
Every holes or..
openings...

572
00:27:28,646 --> 00:27:29,312
Openings?

573
00:27:31,437 --> 00:27:32,312
Listen, son.

574
00:27:33,562 --> 00:27:36,187
The human body
has plenty of holes...

575
00:27:36,271 --> 00:27:38,729
where a tiny hard drive
could be hidden.

576
00:27:38,854 --> 00:27:40,604
This idiot was an expert at that.

577
00:27:41,229 --> 00:27:42,271
No, I...

578
00:27:42,437 --> 00:27:44,604
Why be shy?
He's already dead.

579
00:27:45,604 --> 00:27:46,021
Come on.

580
00:27:47,354 --> 00:27:47,729
Okay.

581
00:27:51,271 --> 00:27:52,729
Use your other hand.

582
00:27:56,312 --> 00:27:56,812
Ugh!

583
00:27:57,854 --> 00:27:58,354
Did you find it?

584
00:27:59,021 --> 00:28:00,146
No.

585
00:28:03,896 --> 00:28:05,229
Sorry, brother.
Forgive me.

586
00:28:05,854 --> 00:28:07,479
Ew! Yuck!

587
00:28:07,562 --> 00:28:08,604
- What are you doing?
- No, I...

588
00:28:08,812 --> 00:28:10,687
He told me to do it. I...

589
00:28:10,729 --> 00:28:11,687
Don't touch me.

590
00:28:12,646 --> 00:28:14,604
Everyone there is petrified,
while you

591
00:28:15,146 --> 00:28:16,229
are messing with the dead body.

592
00:28:16,271 --> 00:28:17,812
I wasn't messing with it.

593
00:28:19,104 --> 00:28:19,771
I am leaving.

594
00:28:19,771 --> 00:28:20,854
No, please listen to me.

595
00:28:20,937 --> 00:28:22,604
Please listen to me.

596
00:28:22,979 --> 00:28:23,812
Hear me out.

597
00:28:24,437 --> 00:28:26,812
Look at this.
Our blackmailer...

598
00:28:26,979 --> 00:28:28,812
is the mastermind
behind the MLA's kidnapping.

599
00:28:30,229 --> 00:28:30,729
Watch.

600
00:28:32,271 --> 00:28:34,187
That man had
a hard drive.

601
00:28:34,396 --> 00:28:36,396
I was searching for it.

602
00:28:37,354 --> 00:28:39,104
This video could
destroy my career.

603
00:28:39,979 --> 00:28:41,104
Who could be behind this?

604
00:28:42,979 --> 00:28:43,687
Whoever he is...

605
00:28:44,187 --> 00:28:45,104
he's a vicious genius.

606
00:28:46,104 --> 00:28:47,437
He has a hundred ways
to strike us...

607
00:28:48,062 --> 00:28:48,979
while we...

608
00:28:49,854 --> 00:28:50,812
have none.

609
00:28:51,896 --> 00:28:53,312
'Regardless of how smart they are,'

610
00:28:54,562 --> 00:28:56,187
'madam will fix them.'

611
00:28:56,354 --> 00:28:57,646
Madam will fix it.

612
00:28:57,646 --> 00:28:58,937
Before dying, Tuglak

613
00:28:59,187 --> 00:29:00,771
- said something bizarre.
- What?

614
00:29:01,479 --> 00:29:03,104
He mentioned...

615
00:29:04,646 --> 00:29:06,646
He mentioned some madam.

616
00:29:06,646 --> 00:29:08,104
Madam? Which madam?

617
00:29:08,229 --> 00:29:09,687
- Which madam?
- Kashvi? - Yes, sir?

618
00:29:10,604 --> 00:29:12,479
Why are you wasting your time
with him? Go inside.

619
00:29:14,854 --> 00:29:15,521
Mr Shanti,

620
00:29:16,521 --> 00:29:18,312
why is ma'am's clock hanging here?

621
00:29:20,896 --> 00:29:21,729
Does it not look good?
Should I take it off?

622
00:29:21,896 --> 00:29:23,854
- No. It's okay. I...
- Do you want it?

623
00:29:23,896 --> 00:29:25,646
- No. I...
- No. There are plenty here.

624
00:29:27,146 --> 00:29:28,312
We hung the clock
as we got it for free.

625
00:29:28,562 --> 00:29:30,771
It's in every room,
including the washrooms.

626
00:29:31,771 --> 00:29:33,104
You see. It's our nation's tradition

627
00:29:33,396 --> 00:29:33,687
Yes

628
00:29:34,229 --> 00:29:34,896
to accept gifts.

629
00:29:35,396 --> 00:29:36,271
Be it for a wedding,

630
00:29:36,854 --> 00:29:37,687
your birthday

631
00:29:38,479 --> 00:29:39,187
or an election.

632
00:29:39,479 --> 00:29:40,771
We get so many freebies
like this one.

633
00:29:41,562 --> 00:29:44,479
So, if it's for free, it's for me.

634
00:29:45,312 --> 00:29:46,396
Mr Shanti!

635
00:29:46,396 --> 00:29:47,479
I'm coming, sir.

636
00:29:47,896 --> 00:29:49,271
Show your hands.

637
00:29:49,354 --> 00:29:49,979
Yes.

638
00:29:50,437 --> 00:29:51,396
I wonder where those have gone.

639
00:29:52,604 --> 00:29:54,021
MLA Rohit Trivedi

640
00:29:54,646 --> 00:29:56,104
is like a son to me.

641
00:29:57,354 --> 00:29:59,604
The authorities will spare
no effort to bring him back.

642
00:30:01,229 --> 00:30:01,979
As for

643
00:30:02,604 --> 00:30:04,604
those demanding bizarre ransoms,

644
00:30:05,729 --> 00:30:07,396
their intentions may be noble,

645
00:30:08,979 --> 00:30:10,187
but their methods are wrong.

646
00:30:15,104 --> 00:30:15,604
Yes, tell me.

647
00:30:15,646 --> 00:30:16,771
Listen, Splitter.

648
00:30:17,437 --> 00:30:18,604
I'm in serious trouble.

649
00:30:18,937 --> 00:30:20,687
You're the only one
who can help me.

650
00:30:21,937 --> 00:30:23,396
Someone is blackmailing me.

651
00:30:27,646 --> 00:30:29,604
He has CCTV footage
from every camera in the station.

652
00:30:30,854 --> 00:30:32,479
Someone in this station
is working with him.

653
00:30:33,479 --> 00:30:36,271
Everything looks normal...
but it isn't.

654
00:30:37,646 --> 00:30:38,604
Start with her.

655
00:30:40,896 --> 00:30:41,771
She's different.

656
00:30:43,104 --> 00:30:44,896
She's the queen of mistrust.

657
00:30:45,521 --> 00:30:46,896
Something's off, Splitter.

658
00:30:47,312 --> 00:30:49,562
Then there's an inspector...
completely unhinged.

659
00:30:50,104 --> 00:30:51,104
Either he'll sink...

660
00:30:51,604 --> 00:30:52,687
or drag us all down with him.

661
00:30:53,271 --> 00:30:54,896
And then there's the ACP...

662
00:30:55,271 --> 00:30:56,896
calm on the outside,
sharp on the inside.

663
00:30:57,521 --> 00:30:59,104
They're all breathing down my neck.

664
00:30:59,646 --> 00:31:00,604
Jumper...

665
00:31:00,979 --> 00:31:02,479
Listen to me carefully.

666
00:31:03,812 --> 00:31:06,646
The man who's calling you
is no ordinary criminal.

667
00:31:07,646 --> 00:31:08,646
I mean...

668
00:31:09,187 --> 00:31:10,771
you're chasing a cat,
while he's a tiger.

669
00:31:13,479 --> 00:31:15,521
"Splitter? Hello?
What are you saying?"

670
00:31:16,354 --> 00:31:17,979
"What do you mean?"

671
00:31:21,229 --> 00:31:21,854
Tell me Bro...

672
00:31:23,521 --> 00:31:24,771
Couldn't keep it to yourself,
could you?

673
00:31:25,687 --> 00:31:27,271
You told your little sidekick
everything.

674
00:31:30,396 --> 00:31:33,687
A sheep lives in fear
of the wolf...

675
00:31:34,187 --> 00:31:36,229
never realizing it's the shepherd
who'll betray and slaughter it.

676
00:31:38,396 --> 00:31:39,146
'Ah!'

677
00:31:39,771 --> 00:31:42,104
'Jumper, please save me!'

678
00:31:42,437 --> 00:31:44,062
Please save me!

679
00:31:44,812 --> 00:31:47,604
Trust is like
the eraser on a pencil...

680
00:31:47,729 --> 00:31:49,479
it gets smaller
with every mistake.

681
00:31:50,229 --> 00:31:52,396
And now...
you'll pay for yours.

682
00:31:52,937 --> 00:31:54,104
Ah!

683
00:31:54,146 --> 00:31:57,312
'Ah! Johnny, save me!'

684
00:32:28,729 --> 00:32:31,646
'Ah! Johnny, save me!'

685
00:32:32,646 --> 00:32:34,687
'Johnny, please save me, brother.'

686
00:32:35,562 --> 00:32:38,187
'I am Splitter.'

687
00:32:38,271 --> 00:32:40,271
'You are Jumper.
We're both orphans.'

688
00:32:41,979 --> 00:32:44,187
'Johnny, save me!'

689
00:32:44,396 --> 00:32:47,896
'I am Splitter. You are Jumper.
We're both orphans.'

690
00:33:22,937 --> 00:33:25,937
'Despite receiving
two solid leads...'

691
00:33:26,187 --> 00:33:27,729
'on MLA Rohit's kidnappers,'

692
00:33:27,812 --> 00:33:30,604
'both police raids...'

693
00:33:30,646 --> 00:33:32,687
'failed to uncover
a single suspect or any evidence.'

694
00:33:32,729 --> 00:33:35,062
'Who is behind
these crimes?'

695
00:33:35,062 --> 00:33:38,104
'And why did Force of Justice
make this explosive revelation go viral?'

696
00:33:38,437 --> 00:33:40,979
'With the police
still without a suspect...'

697
00:33:41,187 --> 00:33:44,521
'is the kidnapped MLA's
life now in greater danger?'

698
00:33:45,979 --> 00:33:49,437
'What is the local police doing
to bring the MLA home?'

699
00:33:52,521 --> 00:33:53,896
'Questions abound...'

700
00:33:54,021 --> 00:33:55,562
'but there isn't a single answer.'

701
00:33:57,146 --> 00:34:00,646
Mr. Shanti, they escaped
from the last location too.

702
00:34:01,271 --> 00:34:04,521
The next ransom video
will create havoc.

703
00:34:05,937 --> 00:34:07,354
On top of that,
the CBI is on our backs.

704
00:34:08,479 --> 00:34:09,937
We have to catch Tuglak.

705
00:34:10,271 --> 00:34:11,187
Do something, sir.

706
00:34:12,021 --> 00:34:15,854
I know. I understand.
Tuglak is...

707
00:34:16,604 --> 00:34:19,271
the key that unlocks everything.
Think, Mr. Shanti.

708
00:34:20,521 --> 00:34:21,521
Sir, how can you...

709
00:34:21,687 --> 00:34:24,437
be so certain this man
is linked to the kidnapping?

710
00:34:25,729 --> 00:34:28,979
How can you be so certain
he isn't?

711
00:34:29,479 --> 00:34:32,354
Why are we fixated
on just one man?

712
00:34:32,479 --> 00:34:34,187
Experience.

713
00:34:34,479 --> 00:34:35,271
- Experience?
- Yes.

714
00:34:35,354 --> 00:34:36,437
Sir, take a look.

715
00:34:36,896 --> 00:34:38,729
According to these records...

716
00:34:38,771 --> 00:34:41,187
he taught History.
Well, he still does.

717
00:34:41,271 --> 00:34:41,771
Hmm.

718
00:34:42,104 --> 00:34:44,479
He's committed several crimes...

719
00:34:44,646 --> 00:34:45,646
all alone,
in broad daylight.

720
00:34:46,396 --> 00:34:47,062
Really?

721
00:34:48,437 --> 00:34:51,521
That tells me
he doesn't trust people easily.

722
00:34:51,646 --> 00:34:54,271
If he has a team...

723
00:34:54,437 --> 00:34:55,687
it'll be small and ruthless.

724
00:34:55,812 --> 00:34:57,521
With a small team...

725
00:34:57,729 --> 00:34:59,812
he could slip out of the city
posing as a police officer.

726
00:34:59,854 --> 00:35:00,896
How could he pose
as a police officer?

727
00:35:01,521 --> 00:35:03,312
The police have sealed off
every exit.

728
00:35:03,396 --> 00:35:04,354
He can't get out.

729
00:35:05,312 --> 00:35:06,312
But, sir...

730
00:35:08,146 --> 00:35:09,604
he looks suspicious
from head to toe.

731
00:35:10,229 --> 00:35:11,979
His appearance,
his mannerisms...

732
00:35:12,062 --> 00:35:13,312
even his name.
Everything about him is fake.

733
00:35:15,437 --> 00:35:16,729
What do you mean
his name is fake?

734
00:35:21,229 --> 00:35:23,187
- Didn't he teach History?
- Yes.

735
00:35:23,521 --> 00:35:25,687
Every alias he's used...

736
00:35:25,687 --> 00:35:29,104
belongs to a historical king.
Rewind. Open that folder.

737
00:35:31,229 --> 00:35:32,062
Akbar Ali?

738
00:35:33,396 --> 00:35:34,229
Emperor Akbar.

739
00:35:34,604 --> 00:35:35,646
And Ibrahim?

740
00:35:35,979 --> 00:35:37,146
Ibrahim Lodi!

741
00:35:37,812 --> 00:35:39,646
And B. S. Zafar?

742
00:35:43,479 --> 00:35:44,729
Bahadur Shah Zafar.

743
00:35:47,604 --> 00:35:50,562
Brilliant.
You've just given us a breakthrough.

744
00:35:51,104 --> 00:35:52,396
Ms. Kashvi...

745
00:35:53,146 --> 00:35:54,812
Make a list of every phone number...

746
00:35:54,854 --> 00:35:56,854
registered...

747
00:35:56,896 --> 00:35:58,021
- under the names of historical kings.
- Yes, sir.

748
00:36:00,146 --> 00:36:02,562
Sir, there are eleven names...

749
00:36:02,687 --> 00:36:04,062
matching those
of historical kings.

750
00:36:04,396 --> 00:36:06,937
Now compare that list...

751
00:36:06,937 --> 00:36:08,187
with the calls
under ten seconds.

752
00:36:08,312 --> 00:36:09,687
Yes, sir.

753
00:36:10,187 --> 00:36:11,896
Sir, only one name matches.

754
00:36:12,687 --> 00:36:13,646
C. G. Maurya.

755
00:36:15,771 --> 00:36:16,979
"Trespasser!"

756
00:36:19,854 --> 00:36:21,979
C. G. Maurya?

757
00:36:22,812 --> 00:36:23,979
C. G. Maurya?

758
00:36:26,187 --> 00:36:27,396
Chandragupta Maurya!

759
00:36:28,354 --> 00:36:29,812
"That fraud Zafar
lives in T2."

760
00:36:30,271 --> 00:36:32,396
"There are 500 flats here,
all identical."

761
00:36:35,354 --> 00:36:37,979
Sir, wait.
I'll go and bug his apartment.

762
00:36:38,604 --> 00:36:40,729
No. There's no time
for surveillance now.

763
00:36:40,729 --> 00:36:41,687
It's time to strike.

764
00:36:42,146 --> 00:36:45,062
We'll go there and grab Tuglak.
If he's not there...

765
00:36:45,771 --> 00:36:46,771
we'll find something.

766
00:36:47,854 --> 00:36:50,271
DNA, fingerprints...

767
00:36:50,604 --> 00:36:53,979
Anything that leads us
straight to Tuglak.

768
00:36:53,979 --> 00:36:55,562
Sir, I've seen this man.

769
00:36:55,604 --> 00:36:57,521
He looks familiar.

770
00:36:57,896 --> 00:36:59,479
I'm sure he lives
in Chowki Talaiya.

771
00:37:00,312 --> 00:37:02,521
Not in T2.
He lives in S5.

772
00:37:03,771 --> 00:37:05,104
Then we'll check S5 too.

773
00:37:05,729 --> 00:37:08,812
Get the team ready.
Move! We don't have time.

774
00:37:13,146 --> 00:37:15,562
Move! Move!

775
00:37:20,187 --> 00:37:21,979
- Hello.
- You really messed up...

776
00:37:22,812 --> 00:37:23,937
yet your spirit's still intact.

777
00:37:24,312 --> 00:37:25,062
Listen, son.

778
00:37:25,687 --> 00:37:27,562
If you leave the station now...

779
00:37:28,104 --> 00:37:29,979
the police will suspect you.

780
00:37:31,021 --> 00:37:31,854
But if you stay...

781
00:37:32,604 --> 00:37:34,271
- you'll be caught.
- Then help me!

782
00:37:36,646 --> 00:37:38,896
Everyone has to
clean up their own mess.

783
00:37:43,354 --> 00:37:45,979
Hello. My phone died.
No time to charge it.

784
00:37:50,937 --> 00:37:52,021
As the elders say...

785
00:37:53,437 --> 00:37:54,229
Wisdom...

786
00:37:55,062 --> 00:37:56,937
comes only after
stumbling in the dark.

787
00:38:05,979 --> 00:38:06,771
What do we do now?

788
00:38:07,646 --> 00:38:08,896
The police will definitely find...

789
00:38:09,229 --> 00:38:10,979
our DNA and fingerprints.

790
00:38:11,021 --> 00:38:12,854
That's why
I sent them to S5.

791
00:38:13,187 --> 00:38:15,021
What? Have you lost your mind?

792
00:38:15,521 --> 00:38:16,479
They're cops.

793
00:38:17,312 --> 00:38:19,229
It won't take them long...

794
00:38:19,562 --> 00:38:20,854
to find the right address.

795
00:38:20,854 --> 00:38:22,021
I just need ten minutes.

796
00:38:22,312 --> 00:38:24,104
There's a laptop
with the hard drive.

797
00:38:24,104 --> 00:38:26,229
I'll go get it.
You handle things here. Okay?

798
00:39:05,687 --> 00:39:06,396
Oh!

799
00:40:33,979 --> 00:40:35,146
Ma'am, where's Johnny?

800
00:40:35,521 --> 00:40:36,604
Johnny...

801
00:40:37,812 --> 00:40:40,146
He went to the restroom.

802
00:41:20,021 --> 00:41:20,521
Let's go.

803
00:41:44,771 --> 00:41:45,437
Ah!

804
00:41:45,521 --> 00:41:47,104
Oh, gosh!

805
00:41:47,979 --> 00:41:50,812
Sorry, sir.
I thought he was my husband.

806
00:41:51,146 --> 00:41:51,687
Really, ma'am?

807
00:41:52,271 --> 00:41:53,646
At least look properly...

808
00:41:53,646 --> 00:41:55,812
- before you ride on someone.
- It's okay.

809
00:41:56,021 --> 00:41:57,604
Let's go. Head to T2.

810
00:42:01,146 --> 00:42:02,437
- You?
- Yes.

811
00:42:02,479 --> 00:42:04,104
I was tipped off
before the police arrived.

812
00:42:04,187 --> 00:42:06,437
I've wiped out
every trace of evidence.

813
00:42:06,479 --> 00:42:08,146
Aren't you from the station?

814
00:42:08,146 --> 00:42:10,396
Yes, sir.
I'm the cleanup specialist.

815
00:42:10,437 --> 00:42:11,562
Radios, gramophones,

816
00:42:11,562 --> 00:42:14,354
tables, chairs, TVs,
homes, cars...

817
00:42:14,354 --> 00:42:17,437
pickpockets, kidnappings,
extortion, scams...

818
00:42:17,437 --> 00:42:19,146
cover-ups, cleanups...
you name it.

819
00:42:19,187 --> 00:42:20,521
I leave no trace behind.

820
00:42:20,812 --> 00:42:21,687
Bloodstains...

821
00:42:21,937 --> 00:42:23,396
someone's father,
someone's wife...

822
00:42:23,687 --> 00:42:25,729
or someone's property...

823
00:42:25,896 --> 00:42:27,021
I can make
anything disappear.

824
00:42:27,104 --> 00:42:28,354
The police will
soon be here. Let's go.

825
00:42:28,604 --> 00:42:29,312
Run!

826
00:42:29,604 --> 00:42:32,396
The police are on their way.
Move!

827
00:42:40,562 --> 00:42:41,812
Search this place.

828
00:42:41,854 --> 00:42:42,562
Yes.

829
00:42:52,229 --> 00:42:53,979
I see something there.

830
00:42:54,604 --> 00:42:55,604
Move! Faster!

831
00:42:57,521 --> 00:42:57,896
Hey!

832
00:42:59,229 --> 00:43:00,396
Run!

833
00:43:02,021 --> 00:43:02,979
Come on.

834
00:43:08,104 --> 00:43:09,771
Hey!

835
00:43:09,812 --> 00:43:10,771
They got away.

836
00:43:10,812 --> 00:43:13,396
No pain, no gain.
Move aside. Come on!

837
00:43:14,312 --> 00:43:15,604
What are you looking at?
Go! Get him!

838
00:43:16,229 --> 00:43:18,021
Run! Move!

839
00:43:42,229 --> 00:43:42,896
Ow!

840
00:44:21,021 --> 00:44:22,646
Doesn't anyone clean
this filthy place?

841
00:44:23,771 --> 00:44:24,896
What kind of place is this?

842
00:44:25,687 --> 00:44:26,479
Alright, buddy. See you.

843
00:44:27,104 --> 00:44:28,604
- I'm heading out.
- Where's Splitter?

844
00:44:29,896 --> 00:44:32,146
I have no idea
where Splitter is.

845
00:44:33,271 --> 00:44:34,937
I'm asking nicely.

846
00:44:35,187 --> 00:44:38,187
I'm telling you the truth.
I don't know where he is.

847
00:44:39,104 --> 00:44:40,687
Last chance.
Where's Splitter?

848
00:44:40,937 --> 00:44:42,062
Don't you get it?

849
00:44:42,521 --> 00:44:44,354
I'm asking one last time.
Where's Splitter?

850
00:44:45,187 --> 00:44:47,521
How many times do I have to tell you?
I don't know!

851
00:44:47,687 --> 00:44:50,229
Back off, or I'll shoot.
I'm warning you.

852
00:44:50,396 --> 00:44:52,021
- Lower the gun.
- Get out!

853
00:44:52,104 --> 00:44:52,687
Lower it.

854
00:44:53,396 --> 00:44:54,146
I don't know...

855
00:44:54,146 --> 00:44:56,062
Lower the gun!

856
00:44:56,104 --> 00:44:57,896
Get out, or I'll shoot!
I'm warning you!

857
00:44:58,104 --> 00:44:58,854
Hey!

858
00:44:59,354 --> 00:45:00,229
The gun might go off!

859
00:45:00,854 --> 00:45:01,896
The gun might go off!

860
00:45:02,354 --> 00:45:03,729
Do you hear me?

861
00:45:03,812 --> 00:45:05,729
Watch it! The gun will go off!

862
00:45:06,021 --> 00:45:06,812
Let go!

863
00:45:15,146 --> 00:45:17,604
I told you it'd go off.

864
00:45:25,896 --> 00:45:27,187
Aaaah!

865
00:45:36,896 --> 00:45:39,396
Mr. Sharma?

866
00:45:40,854 --> 00:45:42,187
What is your problem?

867
00:45:42,604 --> 00:45:43,896
You killed another one of my men.

868
00:45:44,271 --> 00:45:46,687
You keep making
very expensive mistakes.

869
00:45:47,271 --> 00:45:48,979
Now you'll have to
do his job too.

870
00:45:49,896 --> 00:45:52,271
Your phone is always dead,
but your brain never is.

871
00:45:52,646 --> 00:45:55,854
He was an expert
at erasing fingerprints and evidence.

872
00:45:56,146 --> 00:45:57,354
Now you've erased him.

873
00:46:00,396 --> 00:46:02,771
Go. Get out of there!

874
00:46:24,229 --> 00:46:25,187
Stop!

875
00:46:26,104 --> 00:46:26,979
Stay right there!

876
00:46:34,104 --> 00:46:34,854
Shanti Ji..

877
00:46:35,687 --> 00:46:36,104
Yes, sir?

878
00:46:36,562 --> 00:46:37,604
Come here.

879
00:46:38,312 --> 00:46:39,687
Should I check this lane?

880
00:46:40,312 --> 00:46:42,396
We need to go that way.
Come on.

881
00:46:44,937 --> 00:46:45,396
Okay.

882
00:46:46,854 --> 00:46:47,396
Run!

883
00:46:49,312 --> 00:46:50,812
Look to your left.

884
00:46:51,354 --> 00:46:54,396
"The third ransom video
of MLA Rohit Trivedi..."

885
00:46:54,396 --> 00:46:55,896
"...has just been released."

886
00:47:00,354 --> 00:47:02,479
Despite all the warnings...

887
00:47:04,062 --> 00:47:06,604
you still couldn't catch
a single criminal.

888
00:47:07,979 --> 00:47:08,812
The price...

889
00:47:09,396 --> 00:47:11,021
...will have to be paid.

890
00:47:19,104 --> 00:47:21,854
The MLA will pay
for the deaths of my men.

891
00:47:21,896 --> 00:47:23,604
Next time, it'll be Splitter.

892
00:47:23,896 --> 00:47:24,646
Not his finger...
something far more precious.

893
00:47:32,729 --> 00:47:34,021
This is your last warning.

894
00:47:35,146 --> 00:47:38,062
Go through the back entrance
of the fourth building...

895
00:47:38,104 --> 00:47:39,479
...on the lane ahead and hide.

896
00:47:40,146 --> 00:47:41,187
The police are right behind you.

897
00:48:16,937 --> 00:48:18,562
You're the queen of bargaining.

898
00:48:18,562 --> 00:48:20,729
But you're practically family.

899
00:48:21,479 --> 00:48:23,854
I bought so many sarees from you...

900
00:48:23,896 --> 00:48:25,396
...for Aunt Neena's wedding.

901
00:48:25,937 --> 00:48:27,062
What's this, Karsan?

902
00:48:27,729 --> 00:48:28,646
Ma'am,

903
00:48:28,687 --> 00:48:29,771
you're family to me too.

904
00:48:29,854 --> 00:48:31,979
That's why I'm giving you
a discount for your daughter's wedding.

905
00:48:32,104 --> 00:48:32,729
But...

906
00:48:32,854 --> 00:48:34,396
Alright. No problem.

907
00:48:34,896 --> 00:48:36,854
Then I'll save the bigger discount...

908
00:48:37,062 --> 00:48:38,771
...for your wedding.

909
00:48:54,396 --> 00:48:54,979
Who are you?

910
00:48:55,312 --> 00:48:56,312
- What do you want?
- Sir...

911
00:48:56,437 --> 00:48:58,104
- The police...
- The police are after you?

912
00:48:58,146 --> 00:48:59,729
I didn't do anything, sir.

913
00:48:59,729 --> 00:49:00,812
Then why are they after you?

914
00:49:02,812 --> 00:49:05,271
- If they catch Splitter, my brother...
- Why would...

915
00:49:05,271 --> 00:49:07,146
...the police arrest
and beat your brother?

916
00:49:11,062 --> 00:49:12,396
- Who screamed?
- Get up!

917
00:49:13,729 --> 00:49:14,604
Blood!

918
00:49:14,646 --> 00:49:15,771
What happened?

919
00:49:15,812 --> 00:49:16,354
Blood!

920
00:49:17,187 --> 00:49:19,146
- What happened?
- He went there.

921
00:49:19,187 --> 00:49:20,729
Yes. Check there.

922
00:49:20,771 --> 00:49:22,312
Run! Check there. Hurry up!

923
00:49:42,687 --> 00:49:43,604
Sir, did you...

924
00:49:44,521 --> 00:49:45,687
see a boy run past?

925
00:49:46,271 --> 00:49:48,062
- What?
- He ran this way.

926
00:49:50,729 --> 00:49:51,729
He can't see.

927
00:49:53,021 --> 00:49:53,729
He's blind?

928
00:49:54,604 --> 00:49:55,062
Yes.

929
00:49:55,562 --> 00:49:56,687
Would you like some tea or snacks?

930
00:49:58,354 --> 00:49:59,729
He's offering us tea and snacks.

931
00:50:00,146 --> 00:50:01,021
- Let's go.
- No?

932
00:50:01,312 --> 00:50:02,854
Alright. Maybe next time!

933
00:50:02,896 --> 00:50:03,312
Yes.

934
00:50:44,812 --> 00:50:45,521
Mr. Shanti!

935
00:50:45,812 --> 00:50:47,354
Sir, shall I order
some ginger tea?

936
00:50:47,396 --> 00:50:48,521
- No!
- Then?

937
00:50:49,021 --> 00:50:50,312
Call Mr. Jumper.

938
00:51:06,062 --> 00:51:07,687
- Johnny, open the door!
- Mr. Jumper!

939
00:51:07,729 --> 00:51:09,187
Open the door!

940
00:51:09,521 --> 00:51:10,479
What happened?

941
00:51:10,521 --> 00:51:11,687
Open the door!

942
00:51:11,896 --> 00:51:13,479
Johnny!

943
00:51:13,521 --> 00:51:14,979
Open the door!

944
00:51:15,021 --> 00:51:16,812
Is anyone in there?

945
00:51:16,979 --> 00:51:18,854
- I don't think anyone's home.
- Open the door! Johnny!

946
00:51:19,479 --> 00:51:20,187
- Open the door!
- Come out!

947
00:51:20,479 --> 00:51:21,979
Open the door!

948
00:51:22,396 --> 00:51:24,812
Johnny! Jumper, come out!
The boss wants you.

949
00:51:24,854 --> 00:51:25,854
Hey! Open the door!

950
00:51:25,854 --> 00:51:28,271
The boss is calling you!
What are you doing?

951
00:51:28,646 --> 00:51:30,062
- Mr. Jumper!
- Is he in there or not?

952
00:51:30,104 --> 00:51:31,271
Open the door!

953
00:51:37,479 --> 00:51:38,646
Are you drunk?

954
00:51:39,771 --> 00:51:40,479
Got an upset stomach?

955
00:51:41,896 --> 00:51:43,687
What's wrong with you?
Come on.

956
00:51:48,229 --> 00:51:49,187
Come.

957
00:51:49,896 --> 00:51:50,479
Come.

958
00:51:50,896 --> 00:51:51,771
Move.

959
00:51:53,271 --> 00:51:54,021
Have some water.

960
00:51:59,896 --> 00:52:01,604
We were chasing a suspect.

961
00:52:03,729 --> 00:52:05,937
He knew every alley...

962
00:52:05,979 --> 00:52:07,229
without CCTV coverage.

963
00:52:20,729 --> 00:52:21,979
- Mr. Shanti?
- Sir.

964
00:52:22,896 --> 00:52:24,979
Are there no CCTV cameras
in Chowki Talaiya?

965
00:52:25,354 --> 00:52:25,812
No, sir.

966
00:52:27,646 --> 00:52:28,646
- Why?
- Well...

967
00:52:29,229 --> 00:52:30,562
They do install them.

968
00:52:31,021 --> 00:52:32,479
But there are
so many crooks there...

969
00:52:33,396 --> 00:52:34,771
they're stolen
the very next day.

970
00:52:36,021 --> 00:52:38,771
Fair enough.
Everyone's trying to make a living.

971
00:52:55,896 --> 00:52:58,729
Around Lanes 17 and 46...

972
00:52:59,812 --> 00:53:00,896
there are two ATMs.

973
00:53:01,021 --> 00:53:02,187
- Ms. Kashvi?
- Yes, sir.

974
00:53:02,479 --> 00:53:05,187
Do ATMs have CCTV cameras...

975
00:53:05,229 --> 00:53:07,562
both inside and outside?

976
00:53:10,146 --> 00:53:11,354
Get the footage.

977
00:53:12,854 --> 00:53:13,479
Yes, sir.

978
00:53:19,229 --> 00:53:21,604
In the meantime,
get some rest.

979
00:53:22,229 --> 00:53:23,437
Have some more water.

980
00:53:33,854 --> 00:53:35,604
Make sure he doesn't escape.

981
00:53:36,604 --> 00:53:37,562
Don't worry.

982
00:53:38,437 --> 00:53:40,146
I've got eyes, not CCTV cameras...

983
00:53:40,312 --> 00:53:41,521
No one can rip them out.

984
00:53:53,854 --> 00:53:58,187
'Ah! Johnny, save me!'

985
00:54:00,312 --> 00:54:00,937
Gosh!

986
00:54:13,396 --> 00:54:14,104
What happened?

987
00:54:15,062 --> 00:54:17,146
I accidentally killed another man
who worked for the kidnapper.

988
00:54:17,271 --> 00:54:17,687
What?

989
00:54:20,021 --> 00:54:21,937
But I think the police
have still not found his body.

990
00:54:23,021 --> 00:54:25,146
But how is that possible?

991
00:54:25,687 --> 00:54:26,312
I don't know.

992
00:54:27,271 --> 00:54:29,271
The kidnapper might have hidden it.

993
00:54:29,562 --> 00:54:30,396
That kidnapper?

994
00:54:30,937 --> 00:54:31,896
Was he there?

995
00:54:32,896 --> 00:54:33,812
I don't know.

996
00:54:34,646 --> 00:54:35,437
I didn't recognise him.

997
00:54:36,229 --> 00:54:37,729
But yes. When he walked,

998
00:54:38,312 --> 00:54:39,104
I heard a sound

999
00:54:40,062 --> 00:54:41,354
like there was something

1000
00:54:41,896 --> 00:54:42,854
in his feet.

1001
00:54:46,229 --> 00:54:46,687
He...

1002
00:54:47,979 --> 00:54:50,021
Is he going to kill Splitter..

1003
00:54:53,104 --> 00:54:55,062
He's been taking the beatings
meant for me since we were kids.

1004
00:54:57,104 --> 00:55:00,896
'Ah! You took my share
of the beatings.'

1005
00:55:01,062 --> 00:55:02,687
'Today, I took
your share of beatings.'

1006
00:55:02,771 --> 00:55:04,354
'Tomorrow, you can pay me for it.'

1007
00:55:04,979 --> 00:55:06,604
He got beaten because of me today.

1008
00:55:08,812 --> 00:55:10,312
You know something, Ms. Kashvi?

1009
00:55:11,271 --> 00:55:12,729
I've never had...

1010
00:55:13,854 --> 00:55:15,312
what Splitter always gave me.

1011
00:55:15,604 --> 00:55:16,062
What?

1012
00:55:17,021 --> 00:55:17,521
Hope.

1013
00:55:19,854 --> 00:55:21,396
We had everything.
We were happy.

1014
00:55:22,604 --> 00:55:24,479
But I wanted to be Lord Falkland.

1015
00:55:26,396 --> 00:55:27,604
Look at this.

1016
00:55:28,437 --> 00:55:30,146
I found the kidnapper's phone.

1017
00:55:31,729 --> 00:55:32,771
There's only one contact...

1018
00:55:33,604 --> 00:55:36,437
saved as Sharma.
Do you know who that could be?

1019
00:55:39,396 --> 00:55:41,437
It's not as if...

1020
00:55:41,771 --> 00:55:42,521
you're the only one with problems.

1021
00:55:42,771 --> 00:55:44,312
Everyone has their own.

1022
00:55:46,479 --> 00:55:49,146
I still can't figure out
which man is blackmailing you... - Wait.

1023
00:55:49,187 --> 00:55:49,937
Just a second.

1024
00:55:50,604 --> 00:55:52,104
How do you know
the kidnapper's a man?

1025
00:55:52,187 --> 00:55:53,271
Isn't it obvious?

1026
00:55:53,396 --> 00:55:55,479
- Obvious?
- Have you lost your mind?

1027
00:55:56,437 --> 00:55:58,229
- Are you accusing me?
- No, I...

1028
00:55:58,354 --> 00:55:59,229
I'm not accusing you.

1029
00:55:59,354 --> 00:56:02,062
Johnny, the only way out...

1030
00:56:02,062 --> 00:56:03,187
is to trust each other.

1031
00:56:03,979 --> 00:56:06,229
Ms. Kashvi, I'm really sorry.
My head's been spinning...

1032
00:56:06,396 --> 00:56:08,146
...since this morning.
I can't think straight.

1033
00:56:08,229 --> 00:56:09,604
Just give me a second.

1034
00:56:10,812 --> 00:56:12,937
I'm glad you're here with me.

1035
00:56:12,979 --> 00:56:14,396
I'm really sorry.

1036
00:56:15,312 --> 00:56:15,771
Sorry.

1037
00:56:23,812 --> 00:56:24,312
Yes?

1038
00:56:29,354 --> 00:56:30,187
Are you done, my brother?

1039
00:56:30,604 --> 00:56:32,271
Huh? I...

1040
00:56:32,854 --> 00:56:33,646
If you

1041
00:56:34,187 --> 00:56:35,229
are done with this,

1042
00:56:35,937 --> 00:56:37,312
let's finish what you're here for.

1043
00:56:37,812 --> 00:56:39,021
Yes.

1044
00:56:39,479 --> 00:56:40,062
I'll be right there.

1045
00:56:42,687 --> 00:56:44,187
Oh, my! You, ma'am?

1046
00:56:44,937 --> 00:56:45,729
Sir, that...

1047
00:56:46,187 --> 00:56:48,354
He's just a cable guy.

1048
00:56:49,312 --> 00:56:50,812
Have some standards.

1049
00:56:59,187 --> 00:57:00,521
- Sir?
- Hmm.

1050
00:57:03,437 --> 00:57:04,979
They're getting closer.

1051
00:57:06,062 --> 00:57:06,437
Hmm.

1052
00:57:10,271 --> 00:57:11,854
Mr. Jumper, press Play.

1053
00:57:16,937 --> 00:57:18,187
Watch this footage.

1054
00:57:21,229 --> 00:57:23,479
You can see the crowd reacting.

1055
00:57:23,562 --> 00:57:25,479
But someone is running
through the shadows behind them.

1056
00:57:25,896 --> 00:57:27,312
Do you see that silhouette?

1057
00:57:29,521 --> 00:57:30,104
Pause it.

1058
00:57:31,479 --> 00:57:33,104
There. That's our suspect.

1059
00:57:33,646 --> 00:57:35,896
Can you sharpen it?
Zoom in.

1060
00:57:36,729 --> 00:57:38,562
Sir, I can't zoom in any further.

1061
00:57:39,562 --> 00:57:40,104
No?

1062
00:57:42,354 --> 00:57:43,729
You can see someone running here.

1063
00:57:44,271 --> 00:57:45,354
But he's looking the other way.

1064
00:57:45,646 --> 00:57:47,521
Retrieve the other ATM's video.
Play it.

1065
00:57:47,521 --> 00:57:48,187
Yes, sir.

1066
00:57:48,604 --> 00:57:49,646
We'll have something solid now.

1067
00:57:51,354 --> 00:57:53,187
Who are you?

1068
00:57:55,021 --> 00:57:55,646
Hmm!

1069
00:57:57,979 --> 00:58:00,562
Yes. Can you make
the footage clearer?

1070
00:58:00,729 --> 00:58:03,146
Sir, I can't sharpen it further.

1071
00:58:08,812 --> 00:58:10,146
- Mr Shanti?
- Sir!

1072
00:58:11,479 --> 00:58:13,021
- He looks like him, doesn't he?
- Yes.

1073
00:58:15,437 --> 00:58:17,562
- He's the same one.
- Yes, he's the same one.

1074
00:58:20,312 --> 00:58:21,396
- He's the same guy... the one..
- Who?

1075
00:58:25,437 --> 00:58:25,979
You...

1076
00:58:29,646 --> 00:58:30,021
Me?

1077
00:58:43,646 --> 00:58:44,646
Hmm!

1078
00:58:46,896 --> 00:58:47,604
