01:30:04,812 --> 01:30:06,521
You ended up killing them both.

1621
01:30:06,896 --> 01:30:08,896
But... aren't you blind?

1622
01:30:20,604 --> 01:30:21,729
I told you.

1623
01:30:22,604 --> 01:30:25,312
I see better than
most people with eyesight.

1624
01:30:25,646 --> 01:30:28,271
Sir, why did you frame me
for all this?

1625
01:30:33,437 --> 01:30:34,646
Didn't I tell you, son?

1626
01:30:36,979 --> 01:30:39,271
You were simply
in the wrong place at the wrong time.

1627
01:30:40,396 --> 01:30:42,979
The world needed
the perfect scapegoat...

1628
01:30:43,354 --> 01:30:44,812
and we chose Tuglak.

1629
01:30:47,396 --> 01:30:48,396
"What is Tuglak?"

1630
01:30:51,854 --> 01:30:54,104
"After Tuglak's death,
what was supposed to happen in seven days..."

1631
01:30:54,146 --> 01:30:55,479
"...will now happen in seven hours."

1632
01:30:55,521 --> 01:30:56,604
"There's only one way out."

1633
01:30:56,979 --> 01:30:57,937
"Find Tuglak."

1634
01:30:58,312 --> 01:30:59,229
"Find the MLA."

1635
01:30:59,437 --> 01:31:01,604
"There's a hard drive
hidden in that body. Find it."

1636
01:31:03,312 --> 01:31:05,062
"You're looking for a cat,
but he's a big cat."

1637
01:31:05,479 --> 01:31:05,854
"Run."

1638
01:31:05,896 --> 01:31:08,729
"Before he died,
Tuglak said something strange."

1639
01:31:08,771 --> 01:31:09,396
"What?"

1640
01:31:10,604 --> 01:31:12,604
"He mentioned some woman."

1641
01:31:13,687 --> 01:31:15,479
'Enter through the back door of
the fourth building'

1642
01:31:15,562 --> 01:31:16,937
'on the lane ahead'

1643
01:31:17,687 --> 01:31:18,479
'and hide.'

1644
01:31:20,729 --> 01:31:21,396
'Who is it?'

1645
01:31:22,354 --> 01:31:23,562
'It's neither of them.'

1646
01:31:24,354 --> 01:31:27,396
'The tremor in the ACP's voice
is strange.'

1647
01:31:27,479 --> 01:31:29,896
'I am that crooked frisbee'

1648
01:31:29,896 --> 01:31:32,229
'which hits your backside
after you throw it.'

1649
01:31:50,437 --> 01:31:51,979
What's wrong with you?

1650
01:31:56,562 --> 01:31:57,896
Sorry, sir.

1651
01:31:59,979 --> 01:32:00,687
You see...

1652
01:32:02,146 --> 01:32:02,896
"Karma"

1653
01:32:03,646 --> 01:32:04,604
is like a boomerang.

1654
01:32:06,187 --> 01:32:07,021
If you throw it wrong,

1655
01:32:07,812 --> 01:32:09,104
it comes flying back

1656
01:32:09,437 --> 01:32:10,437
before you know it...

1657
01:32:11,271 --> 01:32:12,396
and hits you instead.

1658
01:32:13,521 --> 01:32:14,312
"Karma?"

1659
01:32:29,312 --> 01:32:30,479
The earbud!

1660
01:32:30,562 --> 01:32:32,271
"How are you going to find me?"

1661
01:32:32,271 --> 01:32:33,562
"Say the code word."

1662
01:32:34,021 --> 01:32:35,896
"It's also used
to track the location."

1663
01:32:36,521 --> 01:32:37,312
"Karma!"

1664
01:33:16,354 --> 01:33:18,271
Pray we never meet again.

1665
01:33:20,479 --> 01:33:21,604
Because if we do...

1666
01:33:24,896 --> 01:33:26,104
I'll finish what I started.

1667
01:33:34,271 --> 01:33:34,854
Take him.

1668
01:34:00,104 --> 01:34:01,354
We finally caught him.

1669
01:34:01,687 --> 01:34:04,021
Sir is here. Hurry up.

1670
01:34:04,229 --> 01:34:05,021
Come on.

1671
01:34:05,396 --> 01:34:07,104
Sit down. Yes.

1672
01:34:07,812 --> 01:34:09,646
Sit! Come on!

1673
01:34:19,562 --> 01:34:20,896
Where's Jumper?

1674
01:34:32,104 --> 01:34:32,979
What are you staring at?

1675
01:34:34,062 --> 01:34:34,521
Sir,

1676
01:34:35,062 --> 01:34:37,104
I still don't understand
the motive behind all this.

1677
01:34:37,687 --> 01:34:38,229
Hmm.

1678
01:34:38,896 --> 01:34:41,062
Why stage a kidnapping
without demanding a ransom?

1679
01:34:43,396 --> 01:34:45,271
Before he died,
Tuglak said something.

1680
01:34:46,271 --> 01:34:46,896
Yeah?

1681
01:34:47,104 --> 01:34:49,604
He hinted at some madam.

1682
01:34:54,104 --> 01:34:55,687
'Regardless of how smart they are,'

1683
01:34:55,771 --> 01:34:57,687
'madam will fix them.'

1684
01:34:58,146 --> 01:35:00,437
'There are no CCTV cameras
or street lights here.'

1685
01:35:00,479 --> 01:35:01,771
'Your man must be there.'

1686
01:35:02,521 --> 01:35:05,479
'He was there on the day
the MLA was kidnapped.'

1687
01:35:06,062 --> 01:35:08,104
'He doesn't trust anyone soon.'

1688
01:35:08,146 --> 01:35:10,854
'If he has a team,
it will be lean and mean.'

1689
01:35:10,896 --> 01:35:12,604
'Why is ma'am's clock hanging here?'

1690
01:35:12,687 --> 01:35:13,771
'We hung the clock
as we got it for free.'

1691
01:35:13,979 --> 01:35:16,729
'There are several holes
in the human body'

1692
01:35:16,729 --> 01:35:19,229
'where this disk
can be hidden easily.'

1693
01:35:22,146 --> 01:35:23,229
Don't you think this clock...

1694
01:35:23,604 --> 01:35:24,479
looks a little odd?

1695
01:35:24,812 --> 01:35:27,687
Odd? How so?

1696
01:35:27,979 --> 01:35:29,187
Isn't it unusually large?

1697
01:35:29,812 --> 01:35:31,229
Exactly.

1698
01:35:34,604 --> 01:35:37,521
The "lady" Tuglak was referring to...

1699
01:35:39,812 --> 01:35:41,312
was this clock. It's got a hidden camera.

1700
01:35:46,229 --> 01:35:47,229
'You know what?'

1701
01:35:48,604 --> 01:35:50,896
'There's one common thing
in tragedy and comedy.'

1702
01:35:53,187 --> 01:35:53,979
'Timing.'

1703
01:35:57,937 --> 01:36:00,479
I never approved
of trafficking children anyway.

1704
01:36:01,812 --> 01:36:02,521
But...

1705
01:36:04,104 --> 01:36:05,812
you should never have dragged them

1706
01:36:05,896 --> 01:36:06,771
into the drug trade.

1707
01:36:13,479 --> 01:36:16,396
What's this?
What happened to your finger?

1708
01:36:16,687 --> 01:36:18,729
Is that a real cut,
or is it makeup?

1709
01:36:23,354 --> 01:36:25,312
"It looks like you're going
to lose this election,"

1710
01:36:26,562 --> 01:36:27,229
"Mr. Rohit."

1711
01:36:30,437 --> 01:36:32,479
"You know...

1712
01:36:34,562 --> 01:36:36,854
the opposition's lies
are more convincing than yours."

1713
01:36:38,104 --> 01:36:40,771
"We need to think outside the box."

1714
01:36:42,812 --> 01:36:44,437
"We need something
to go viral..."

1715
01:36:44,437 --> 01:36:46,812
"...and throw the whole world
into chaos."

1716
01:36:46,896 --> 01:36:48,979
"What spreads the fastest?"

1717
01:36:53,479 --> 01:36:54,312
"Propaganda."

1718
01:36:56,937 --> 01:36:59,437
"A lie packaged well."

1719
01:37:02,271 --> 01:37:03,771
"The script's ready.
Take a look, sir."

1720
01:37:05,521 --> 01:37:06,562
"It'll be even better..."

1721
01:37:07,437 --> 01:37:08,854
"...when all three locations
are raided..."

1722
01:37:11,104 --> 01:37:12,146
"...and ma'am..."

1723
01:37:16,312 --> 01:37:18,271
All this... just to win an election?

1724
01:37:20,271 --> 01:37:23,646
You had your own husband
hacked to pieces for votes.

1725
01:37:25,354 --> 01:37:27,646
I only had a finger cut off.

1726
01:37:29,312 --> 01:37:31,062
And I walked away untouched.

1727
01:37:31,312 --> 01:37:33,062
My name never surfaced.

1728
01:37:33,146 --> 01:37:35,979
"In a game this dirty..."

1729
01:37:37,312 --> 01:37:39,437
"...conscience is a liability."

1730
01:37:39,979 --> 01:37:41,812
"Another breaking news update."

1731
01:37:41,854 --> 01:37:45,187
"Police have raided two locations
linked to the ransom videos."

1732
01:37:45,229 --> 01:37:47,646
"The illegal operations
uncovered there..."

1733
01:37:47,812 --> 01:37:51,229
"...are allegedly connected to ma'am,
according to the NCB and CBI."

1734
01:37:52,062 --> 01:37:55,062
"Is MLA Rohit Trivedi gaining
even more public support?"

1735
01:37:55,562 --> 01:37:58,729
"Will the people choose him
as the true leader of the youth?"

1736
01:37:58,729 --> 01:38:00,771
You sick bastard!

1737
01:38:00,979 --> 01:38:02,312
What did I ever do to you?

1738
01:38:05,354 --> 01:38:06,896
"Zafar."
"Yes, sir."

1739
01:38:06,937 --> 01:38:09,437
"Don't they use eye drops
to make actors cry on TV?"

1740
01:38:09,812 --> 01:38:10,812
"We don't have any, sir."

1741
01:38:10,896 --> 01:38:12,187
"What kind of production is this?"

1742
01:38:12,937 --> 01:38:14,229
"Won't people notice
if I don't cry?"

1743
01:38:14,396 --> 01:38:16,187
So Shaktimaan was Gangadhar
all along.

1744
01:38:16,812 --> 01:38:17,979
The public will make sure...

1745
01:38:19,104 --> 01:38:20,396
...he ends up as Gangadhar again.

1746
01:38:22,437 --> 01:38:23,979
Sir, I've got an idea.

1747
01:38:24,187 --> 01:38:24,646
What is it?

1748
01:38:31,187 --> 01:38:32,562
"Exclusive of the year!"

1749
01:38:32,646 --> 01:38:34,854
"Prominent MLA Rohit Trivedi..."

1750
01:38:34,896 --> 01:38:37,146
"...orchestrated his own kidnapping."

1751
01:38:37,521 --> 01:38:40,896
"His true colors have now been
exposed before the public."

1752
01:38:41,812 --> 01:38:44,187
"We've obtained shocking footage."
"Hey! Cut!"

1753
01:38:45,271 --> 01:38:46,021
"The dialogue?"

1754
01:38:46,604 --> 01:38:47,479
"Here, sir."

1755
01:38:48,229 --> 01:38:50,646
"Come on. Step closer."

1756
01:38:51,396 --> 01:38:53,646
"Not that close.
Sit here and do it. Come."

1757
01:38:55,271 --> 01:38:57,646
"As you can clearly see
in the footage..."

1758
01:38:57,687 --> 01:39:00,062
"...this entire criminal operation
was masterminded by the MLA..."

1759
01:39:00,062 --> 01:39:02,479
"...to gain public sympathy.
What a shocking scam!"

1760
01:39:03,062 --> 01:39:03,479
"That's right."

1761
01:39:03,812 --> 01:39:04,646
"According to the police..."

1762
01:39:04,729 --> 01:39:06,687
"...four people were involved
in the kidnapping..."

1763
01:39:06,937 --> 01:39:08,771
"...Mr. Sharma, Rajesh Kansal..."

1764
01:39:09,271 --> 01:39:11,354
"...Tuglak, and the cleaner, Shukla."

1765
01:39:11,771 --> 01:39:14,396
"Two of the accused died..."

1766
01:39:14,437 --> 01:39:15,229
"...in an internal feud."

1767
01:39:15,562 --> 01:39:17,937
"Under the leadership
of ACP Karan Veer Gupta..."

1768
01:39:18,062 --> 01:39:20,146
"...the police cracked the case..."

1769
01:39:20,146 --> 01:39:22,896
"...with remarkable efficiency
in just 11 hours."

1770
01:39:22,937 --> 01:39:25,104
Nothing is impossible
when you give it your all.

1771
01:39:26,854 --> 01:39:29,312
The case was solved
in under 24 hours.

1772
01:39:32,062 --> 01:39:34,021
But that's alright.
I won't take...

1773
01:39:34,854 --> 01:39:36,604
all the credit for it.
It's all because...

1774
01:39:38,396 --> 01:39:39,187
I was...

1775
01:39:40,687 --> 01:39:42,687
I was always by their side.

1776
01:39:43,187 --> 01:39:45,021
I still am, and always will be.

1777
01:39:45,729 --> 01:39:47,146
Without me...

1778
01:39:47,979 --> 01:39:49,437
Jai Hind!

1779
01:39:50,021 --> 01:39:52,896
ACP Karma took
all the credit.

1780
01:39:53,146 --> 01:39:54,812
Didn't that bother you?

1781
01:39:58,437 --> 01:40:00,062
Your car carried
two dead bodies.

1782
01:40:01,271 --> 01:40:02,521
That was the price I paid.

1783
01:40:03,979 --> 01:40:06,687
Was it a price...
or did the ACP outplay you?

1784
01:40:11,271 --> 01:40:12,979
Four thieves and one mastermind...

1785
01:40:13,562 --> 01:40:15,604
...created all this chaos.

1786
01:40:17,354 --> 01:40:19,562
But one thing still puzzles me.

1787
01:40:20,146 --> 01:40:21,104
Why was Sharma...

1788
01:40:21,354 --> 01:40:24,104
...searching Tuglak's corpse
for a hard drive?

1789
01:40:25,104 --> 01:40:25,896
Well, ma'am...

1790
01:40:26,771 --> 01:40:29,104
it all comes down
to money and greed.

1791
01:40:30,437 --> 01:40:32,604
Tuglak was planning to run off...

1792
01:40:33,062 --> 01:40:33,896
...with all their money.

1793
01:40:34,062 --> 01:40:35,187
Their money?

1794
01:40:35,229 --> 01:40:36,187
Stored on a hard drive?

1795
01:40:37,104 --> 01:40:38,104
Where is it now?

1796
01:40:39,104 --> 01:40:40,687
I expected it
to be much bigger.

1797
01:40:41,062 --> 01:40:41,812
Turns out...

1798
01:40:42,979 --> 01:40:43,687
...it's this tiny.

1799
01:40:44,312 --> 01:40:47,312
What? Did Tuglak hide it
inside his mouth?

1800
01:40:47,896 --> 01:40:50,812
It fell in Tuglak's room
just before he died.

1801
01:40:51,396 --> 01:40:52,729
The cleaner found it...

1802
01:40:53,812 --> 01:40:55,187
...and hid it in his phone.

1803
01:40:56,562 --> 01:40:57,521
After he died...

1804
01:40:58,146 --> 01:40:59,396
...I got the phone.

1805
01:41:00,729 --> 01:41:01,312
Oh!

1806
01:41:01,979 --> 01:41:03,187
What's on the hard drive?

1807
01:41:03,729 --> 01:41:04,396
Bitcoin.

1808
01:41:04,854 --> 01:41:05,687
Bitcoin?

1809
01:41:06,146 --> 01:41:06,979
You mean money?

1810
01:41:08,437 --> 01:41:10,021
How much is it worth?

1811
01:41:11,021 --> 01:41:13,271
About two years ago,
it was worth around ₹2 lakhs.

1812
01:41:14,146 --> 01:41:15,312
₹2 lakhs?

1813
01:41:17,271 --> 01:41:19,604
But now...

1814
01:41:20,146 --> 01:41:20,979
...it's worth...

1815
01:41:21,854 --> 01:41:22,896
₹100 crores.

1816
01:41:23,771 --> 01:41:24,396
₹100 crores.

1817
01:41:24,979 --> 01:41:25,896
What?

1818
01:41:26,437 --> 01:41:28,187
₹100 crores?

1819
01:41:30,104 --> 01:41:31,146
₹100 crores!

1820
01:41:31,354 --> 01:41:32,771
So what are you going to do...

1821
01:41:34,146 --> 01:41:34,979
...with all that money?

1822
01:41:35,312 --> 01:41:37,396
I've got one hell
of a wicked plan.

1823
01:41:40,479 --> 01:41:41,104
Want to hear it?

1824
01:41:42,729 --> 01:41:44,604
Answer the phone.
Go ahead.

1825
01:41:44,729 --> 01:41:46,354
The ant has grown wings now.

1826
01:41:47,604 --> 01:41:49,562
- Answer the phone, Jumper.
- He's not picking up?

1827
01:41:49,771 --> 01:41:51,937
Mr. Shanti, I'm done
with these cable guys.

1828
01:41:51,937 --> 01:41:53,396
Who even uses cable anymore?

1829
01:41:54,146 --> 01:41:54,729
You're right.

1830
01:41:54,729 --> 01:41:57,062
Yeah. Time to move
to the next level.

1831
01:41:57,396 --> 01:41:59,604
- Find the movies online.
- Yes, sir.

1832
01:41:59,604 --> 01:42:00,396
But why?

1833
01:42:01,104 --> 01:42:02,104
Because we have to.

1834
01:42:02,354 --> 01:42:03,021
Got it.

1835
01:42:03,104 --> 01:42:04,687
Now we need an "ant"...

1836
01:42:04,687 --> 01:42:06,604
who not only catches criminals...

1837
01:42:07,146 --> 01:42:09,562
- but can track them too.
- Sir...

1838
01:42:10,312 --> 01:42:13,021
Tracking criminals
is part of our job.

1839
01:42:13,187 --> 01:42:14,604
You forgot the coriander.

1840
01:42:15,479 --> 01:42:16,271
I told you...

1841
01:42:16,729 --> 01:42:17,521
to buy some.

1842
01:42:17,687 --> 01:42:18,812
No problem.

1843
01:42:18,854 --> 01:42:19,937
- I'll get it in two minutes.
- No.

1844
01:42:19,937 --> 01:42:20,979
- Forget it.
- Get in the car. I'll go.

1845
01:42:21,062 --> 01:42:21,854
No, you get in.

1846
01:42:25,854 --> 01:42:27,146
- Sir?
- Hmm?

1847
01:42:28,479 --> 01:42:29,771
Where are we going to find...

1848
01:42:30,271 --> 01:42:32,187
an "ant" who can track criminals?

1849
01:42:33,271 --> 01:42:34,354
We'll find one.

1850
01:42:35,062 --> 01:42:36,437
- You think so?
- We will.

1851
01:42:36,937 --> 01:42:37,479
Definitely.

1852
01:42:39,979 --> 01:42:42,604
Hmm?

1853
01:43:07,187 --> 01:43:08,562
"Jumper!"

1854
01:43:09,979 --> 01:43:11,396
"Jumper!"

1855
01:43:12,771 --> 01:43:14,146
"Jumper!"

1856
01:43:15,229 --> 01:43:16,896
"Johnny Jumper!"

1857
01:43:21,896 --> 01:43:23,021
"Jumper!"

1858
01:43:25,146 --> 01:43:26,396
"Jumper!"

1859
01:43:27,604 --> 01:43:28,979
"Johnny Jumper!"

